BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20230219T220000Z
DTEND:20230220T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:4p31ksoh9jnfcpajvpdcb234p9@google.com
CREATED:20230204T172747Z
DESCRIPTION:Talk- 3:00-4:00<br>Tour- 4:00-5 ish<br>Sign up here- <a href="h
 ttps://www.eventbrite.com/e/artist-talk-at-the-firehouse-tickets-5170045334
 77">https://www.eventbrite.com/e/artist-talk-at-the-firehouse-tickets-51700
 4533477</a><br><br><p>Firehouse artist talks give the community a chance to
  delve deeper into the artist's creative process. They offer the artists an
  opportunity to share background information allowing viewers to gain a bet
 ter understanding of the art on the gallery walls. Attendees are welcome to
  ask questions at the end of the talk\, as well as tour the new exhibit wit
 h the artist at the end of the talk.</p><p></p><p>STITCHED: Connecting Comm
 unity Through Abstraction features the work of Nancy Eastman\, who confront
 s communal values and relationships to the local environment through colorf
 ul mediums and stylized threadwork. Eastman responds to the changing landsc
 apes around both her and the Longmont community through found objects such
 as agricultural fencing\, organic materials such as fallen branches\, and c
 ollaged local imagery to invite the viewer to reflect upon the memories we
 collectively share through our environment.</p><p>SOUTH GALLERY: TEXTURED:
 Curated by Nancy Eastman</p><p>Featuring collaborative monoprints by Patric
 ia Aaron and Alicia McKim and textured and beaded works by Diane Deyo.</p><
 p>Patricia Aaron is an American painter best known for her gestural abstrac
 t landscapes composed of rich layers of encaustic pigments and mixed media
 applied to custom birch panels in her signature style painting technique. A
 aron’s paintings fuse the raw beauty of nature\, earthscapes\, and urban cu
 lture.</p><p>Alicia McKim is a printmaker and book artist living in Denver\
 , CO. For over twenty years\, her work centered around written language\; h
 owever\, post-pandemic\, her work focuses more on the concept of Place.</p>
 <p>Masks and Beaded Works by Diane Deyo</p><p>Diane Deyo has lived in Bould
 er\, Colorado for over thirty years. A former professor of textile design a
 t the University of Northern Colorado and Central Michigan University\, her
  degrees include both a Bachelor and a Master of Fine Arts. She also was an
  art teacher in the Boulder Valley Schools for seventeen years.</p><p>Her c
 urrent work makes use of a distinctive technique which she developed hersel
 f. Using a blend of paint\, oil pastel and colored pencil\, Diane creates h
 er own unique interpretation of the natural world from which she derives he
 r inspiration. Her art reflects her love of nature and travel. These pieces
  are reflections of travels to Africa\, combining pattern and form found in
  traditional African fabrics\, masks and ceremonies. Materials include\, ac
 rylic\, oil pastel\, beads\, and found objects</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230204T172747Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Artist Talk and Tour with Nancy Eastman\, Diane Deyo\, Alicia McKin
 \, and Patricia Aaron
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
