DESCRIPTION:Sign up here: <a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/drawing-and
 -creative-flow-drawing-on-the-right-side-of-the-brain-tickets-904910681207?
 aff=efbevent&amp\;fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAAR0MHxLjSpAyxO10alTpcsTl5MtvcLJv
 KKYDdz9sMGoJEZKnm1M_VAfooVQ_aem_AUNLV87BgYaUrMM-6hT4a6lCsIdDphLpobebiHdR0BZ
 9QQNpOr9LH0oxYo2jo8Rj0D3wVsYgPA2QJLsedKt46Ots">Drawing and Creative Flow: D
 rawing on the right side of the brain Tickets\, Fri\, Jun 14\, 2024 at 2:00
  PM | Eventbrite</a><br><br>Drawing and Creative Flow: Drawing on the right
  side of the brain with Nicolette Toussaint<br><br>Drawing and Creative Flo
 w: Drawing on the right side of the brain<br>This is two-hour class designe
 d for beginning  artists\, those who think "I can't draw" or "I have no art
 istic talent”. The  teaching is rooted in the work of Betty Edwards\, who w
 rote the famed  book "Drawing on the Right Side of the Brain."<br>The point
  of Edwards' teaching - and this class - is to get your noisy\, verbal\, bo
 ssy left brain to let go. The class is designed to get you "into the  zone"
  where your right brain functions. That zone is where dancers\,  musicians\
 , and artists go to create. Getting into your right brain is like a  mini-v
 acation\, and you’ll be surprised at how well good work turns out!<br><br>S
 UPPLIES NEEDED<br>All that's needed are supplies you probably have around t
 he house:<br>• White paper\, could be drawing paper or white typing/copy pa
 per<br>will do<br>• A soft pencil with a good point (it would be nice to ha
 ve an HB\, a<br>2B\, a 4B and a 6B\, but a #2 pencil will do in a pinch)<br
 >• A pencil sharpener<br>• A clean eraser (test it and make sure it doesn't
  leave marks on the  paper\; if it does\, wash it with some hand soap)<br>•
  A ruler or other straight edge
