DESCRIPTION:Introducing our Summer Resident Makenzie Davis!!!\nSummer on th
 e Streets: Papermaking Workshops - July 8th\, August 12th\nThese community
 based papermaking workshops will explore the landscape of Longmont by means
  of two papermaking methods: the pulled sheet and the poured sheet. Partici
 pants will be using paper pulp collected from the community to pull their o
 wn unique sheets of paper in a more traditional method\, adding paint\, nat
 ural pigments\, and plants as part of the process. Additionally\, participa
 nts will work together on a large\, collaborative sheet of poured paper tha
 t will be integrated into Makenzie’s final exhibition at the Firehouse Art
 Center’s Main Gallery in September.\n\nMaterials that the community can con
 tribute before the workshop include:\n- Newspaper\n- Junk mail\n- Scrap pap
 er (from notebooks\, sticky notes\, etc.)\n- Any paper detritus that would
 otherwise be thrown away\n\nIt’s helpful if this paper is shredded or torn
 up into smaller pieces when delivered to the Firehouse\, but it does not ne
 ed to be (there will be additional events that focus on just preparing the
 paper for pulp and sharing stories). Regardless of how the paper is donated
 \, it will be ready for use in the workshops\, where participants will expl
 ore the versatile nature of papermaking as well as a way to connect and bui
 ld community.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230607T001641Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Exhibit Reception/Artist in Residence Workshop during Summer on the
  Streets
