DESCRIPTION:For more information: <a href="https://www.longmontcolorado.gov
 /departments/departments-e-m/museum/education/day-of-the-dead"><u>https://w
 ww.longmontcolorado.gov/departments/departments-e-m/museum/education/day-of
 -the-dead</u></a><b><br></b><br><b><br></b><br><b>11:00am-3:00pm: </b>Festi
 val <br><b>2:00pm-3:00pm:</b> Gigantes Procession <br><br>Día de Muertos (D
 ay of the Dead) is a time to celebrate our deceased loved ones and keep the
 ir memories alive. Running since the year 2000\, it’s the longest-standing
 Day of the Dead exhibition and celebration in Colorado and attracts more th
 an 6\,000 people annually. Community participation is an essential part of
 this holiday full of life\, reflection\, food\, family\, and fun.
