UID:ffcofdn9eierqtqm14abe6c3k0@google.com
CREATED:20200822T054313Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Wednesday: 12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (by appointment only- email in
 fo@firehouseart.org 24 hours in advance to schedule)</p><p>Thursday: 12:00
 pm – 5:00 pm (by appointment only- email info@firehouseart.org 24 hours in
 advance to schedule)</p><p>Friday: 12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (by appointment only-
  email info@firehouseart.org 24 hours in advance to schedule)</p><p>Sunday:
  12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (by appointment only- email info@firehouseart.org 24 ho
 urs in advance to schedule)</p><p>The Firehouse is so excited to be opening
  for weekday appointments\, and with a 5 person capacity on Saturdays. I ha
 ve been receiving questions regarding safety and what to expect at the gall
 ery (from staff as well as the community) as we reopen. Sorry for the long
 post in advance.</p><p>Appointments- Sunday and Wednesday through Friday\,
 guests can request a time to visit between 12pm and 5pm.&nbsp\; Appointment
 s can be made by emailing info@firehouseart.org.&nbsp\; Someone will email
 back confirming your time slot as well as safety procedures.</p><p>Saturday
  – There is a 5 person limit in the gallery. You will be allowed to enter b
 etween 12pm-5pm as capacity permits.</p><p>We are so excited to share these
  works with you\, and we have implemented some safety precautions to keep o
 ur community safe as well as prevent the spread of COVID-19. We ask that if
  you are exhibiting any symptoms of COVID-19 (fever\, cough\, shortness of
 breath) that you stay home except to seek medical help.</p><p>1. Deep clean
 - The Firehouse was deep cleaned before reopening.</p><p>2. Masks- All gues
 ts must follow mandatory state requirements for masks. If you do not have a
  mask\, they are available at the Firehouse for a $5 donation. We will not
 be allowing guests to enter without a mask\, so please be prepared.<br>Your
  cloth face covering should:<br>Reach above the nose\, below the chin\, and
  completely cover the mouth and nostrils<br>Fit snugly against the sides of
  the face<br>Be made of multiple layers of fabric that you can still breath
 e through<br>Be able to be laundered and machine dried without damaging the
  material or shape<br>Learn more at&nbsp\;<a href="https://l.facebook.com/l
 .php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fbit.ly%2F2Ravt42%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR0ZLNqI2f4fGXZGIw3O4RQq
 OpkcKPWE5BByKMdLRliBv2oELZ24McC_4VI&amp\;h=AT1dbZa4ScpJou1nVrlsRDfPz4UE_h1Q
 SWHuaZo5i4nh9bHRdEPjXQfizhiS69d2aqVt5GBmdWGmTBF9Wmn-cLRhEssG8h5sP8-Qv0IOWwY
 EehBOY3cXcnd06XhgiJavcFxdSfSxt79ro-9FBnVGjhbBdfGkJrsh8IFB2ACGgZggn0N-58_L3q
 5UkL5pJn6woKCkN6pl8Hws8yXnVyI_4vm34WISSc40Vej17fWRTM6YRPma9GPMHZPwPcVhOzEGa
 o0yX7YQLpHtNK1sA1U-lC6ig5OyY9OaU6NCtBZMJFNx8-h5V53Docj5OZGlGr_cIyo9HI-YeMQY
 8-3yW21f13HlFUWnsauITdj0h9lp2lebi688MdBPSf3NizG90KHZmqjAg4X6hLLVEtzdzwGew0o
 xlhWLEPFSul8KllW1c2EIVqDrLSk8uYVXVQvbkr5sUFp8YUvgdbva-F-5BNQNCWb7f7yEbgwySd
 vYkCNRAw9tJvEhV-w3Pf9BXOqQJbQ4AsYrYznFNtnl5Im4auLUlAsMLNKrFh-VCDCrtMnrsn6Jv
 2DL6Ef7-1OO8owIIAXWPkH_lsSOSXnWqZsPD5TuxpC9tfgAZHvwXAm1dzDDA8CVU3Wq4o8Nlv4v
 wHbjzxnkJQ">https://bit.ly/2Ravt42</a></p><p>3. Viewing and learning about
 the artwork- Please follow the directional arrows for viewing the artwork.<
 /p><p>4. Please keep staff and volunteers in mind- If you have questions ab
 out the gallery or the artwork\, we welcome them! Please feel free to ask q
 uestions at an appropriate six foot distance to protect our staff and volun
 teers.</p><p>5. What we are doing to keep you safe- Staff and volunteers wi
 ll wear masks during appointments/weekend open times\, as well as sterilize
  surfaces and wash hands after every appointment/every 30 minutes. Antibact
 erial gel is available to guests at different stations throughout the galle
 ry.</p><p>We are excited for you to come see the show and we appreciate you
 r cooperation on our new policies as we move forward with reopening!<br>– E
 laine Waterman<br></p><p>Executive Director</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20210213T223330Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Gallery Open for appointment only
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
