CREATED:20211127T193400Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>Alcohol Ink<br></b>Saturday\, March 26 - noon to
 3 p.m.<br>Learn to create abstract pieces of alcohol ink artwork. We will s
 tart with a ceramic magnet\, then create a greeting card. All materials wil
 l be provided and the class is $40 at Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue
 \, Longmont\, CO 80501.&nbsp\;If you would like to bring your own alcohol i
 nk (in specific colors you like)\, you are welcome to! RSVP at&nbsp\;<a hre
 f="http://prettynicecreations.com/event">prettynicecreations.com/event</a>&
 nbsp\;to save your seat.<br>&nbsp\;<br><b>Pine Needle Basket Weaving</b><br
 >Saturday\, April 9 - noon to 3 p.m.<br><br>Use pine needles and waxed line
 n to weave together baskets using our step-by-step instructions/demonstrati
 on. Rachel Courtney and Dana Steiner will lead the class. All materials wil
 l be provided and the class is $40 at Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue
 \, Longmont\, CO 80501. RSVP at&nbsp\;<a href="http://prettynicecreations.c
 om/event">prettynicecreations.com/event</a>&nbsp\;to save your seat.<br><br
 ><b>Bio</b><br>Rachel Courtney has been interested in designing and creatin
 g art from a young age. She has been making hand-made jewelry\, blankets an
 d scarves for decades and recently started painting. She started crocheting
  in 2000 and has been making blankets for Project Linus ever since. She lau
 nched her Etsy store for Pretty Nice Creations in 2010 and has grown her on
 line selling from scarves and blankets to a wide variety of crafts and grap
 hic design work. She enjoys giving crafting classes – alcohol ink\, jewelry
  making\, painting and more.<br><br>Rachel received a bachelor’s degree in
 journalism and mass communications in 2003 and a certificate in digital gra
 phics technology in 2004. Her love of the simple beauties in life led to th
 e founding of her graphic design company\, Pretty Nice Creations where she
 can share her designs with the world. Beyond her graphics and textile work\
 , Rachel is an accomplished photographer and marketing expert who helps loc
 al businesses grow their reach online and off.</html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220306T182545Z
LOCATION:firehouse art center
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Alcohol Ink- With Rachel Courtney- Main Gallery
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
