 983" __is_owner="true">Slay the Runway | ATLAS Institute | University of Co
 lorado Boulder</a><br><br><p>Slay the Runway offers fashion design\, perfor
 mance&nbsp\;and sewing classes for LGBTQIA+ teens at&nbsp\;<a href="https:/
 /firehouseart.org/">Longmont's Firehouse Art Center</a>&nbsp\;and Boulder P
 ublic Library's Building 61 Maker Space.&nbsp\;At the conclusion of an eigh
 t-week session\,&nbsp\;students participate in a professionally produced ru
 nway show premiering in the ATLAS Institute's B2 Center for Media\, Arts&nb
 sp\;and Performance. In addition to garment construction and design\, parti
 cipants will work with make-up artists and choreographers to refine their d
 ebuts. One night only\, Slay the Runway will feature stunning fashion and o
 riginal performances and collaborations with Twirling Tech Goddess LeeLee J
 ames. This project was made possible by a grant from the&nbsp\;<a href="htt
 ps://oedit.colorado.gov/arts-in-society-grant">Arts in Society Fund</a>.</p
