DTEND:20220122T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:01musvic16or7mqn0f0drpkchq@google.com
CREATED:20211127T201838Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><b>Pine Needle Basket Weaving</b><br>Saturday\, Jan. 22 - n
 oon to 3 p.m.<br><br>Use pine needles and waxed linen to weave together bas
 kets using our step-by-step instructions/demonstration. Rachel Courtney and
  Dana Steiner will lead the class. All materials will be provided and the c
 lass is $40 at Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue\, Longmont\, CO 80501.
  RSVP at&nbsp\;<a href="http://prettynicecreations.com/event">prettynicecre
 ations.com/event</a>&nbsp\;to save your seat.<br><br><b>Lino Block Printing
 <br></b><br>Saturday\, Feb. 5 - noon to 3 p.m.<br>Join Rachel Courtney and
 Dana Steiner for a block painting class. Use blocks\, cutters and brayers t
 o create a reusable relief print of your own creation. All materials will b
 e provided and the class is $40 at Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue\,
 Longmont\, CO 80501.&nbsp\;RSVP at&nbsp\;<a href="http://prettynicecreation
 s.com/event">prettynicecreations.com/event</a>. Students will have the oppo
 rtunity to make 2 designs on 4x6 lino. Bring any sketches you may need to c
 omplete them\, they can be cut into smaller sizes\, you can draw straight o
 n to the lino\, or free cut the designs.<br><br><b>Needle Felted Goats Milk
  Soap Workshop</b><br>Saturday\, Feb. 26 - noon to 3 p.m.<br>Felted soaps a
 re a functional soap with an artistic scrubby built in! When your soap is s
 pent you will be left with a little wool felted pouch that you can poke a h
 ole in and add new soap\, use it to hold potpourri\, air plants or coins. T
 his class is geared towards beginners but fun for felters of any experience
  level. This class includes an unscented goats milk soap\, wool and tools t
 o complete a single felted soap. All materials will be provided and the cla
 ss is $40 at Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue\, Longmont\, CO 80501. R
 SVP at&nbsp\;<a href="http://prettynicecreations.com/event">prettynicecreat
 ions.com/event</a>&nbsp\;to save your seat.<br><br><b>Bio</b><br>Rachel Cou
 rtney has been interested in designing and creating art from a young age. S
 he has been making hand-made jewelry\, blankets and scarves for decades and
  recently started painting. She started crocheting in 2000 and has been mak
 ing blankets for Project Linus ever since. She launched her Etsy store for
 Pretty Nice Creations in 2010 and has grown her online selling from scarves
  and blankets to a wide variety of crafts and graphic design work. She enjo
 ys giving crafting classes – alcohol ink\, jewelry making\, painting and mo
 re.<br><br>Rachel received a bachelor’s degree in journalism and mass commu
 nications in 2003 and a certificate in digital graphics technology in 2004.
  Her love of the simple beauties in life led to the founding of her graphic
  design company\, Pretty Nice Creations where she can share her designs wit
 h the world. Beyond her graphics and textile work\, Rachel is an accomplish
 ed photographer and marketing expert who helps local businesses grow their
 reach online and off.
LAST-MODIFIED:20211127T201838Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pine Needle Basket Weaving with Rachel- Studio 64
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
