CREATED:20220421T183944Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>December is quickly approaching\, complete with all of its
 holiday madness and eggnog-infused schedule-scrambling. I hope it's treatin
 g you well.<br><br>Since December can quickly get crazy with obligatory tra
 vel and work-place holiday parties\, I decided to keep things chill this mo
 nth. Our December meeting will happen at <b>Wibby Brewing </b>on<b> Friday\
 , December 8th from 6 - 8 PM</b>. Come by for a drink and get to know your
 fellow filmmakers. (That said\, I realize that not everyone is interested i
 n alcohol. I'm trying to figure out a coffeeshop-type of place for us to ha
 ve future meetings\, but unfortunately\, most of those places in Longmont a
 ren't open past 6. However\, I believe Wibby usually has at least one or tw
 o NA options until I can figure out some other hangout spot.)<br><br>A few
 notes for your consideration:<br><ul><li>Thanks so much to all who attended
  and spoke at our November short film panel\, especially to <a href="http:/
 /www.justinjackola.com/">Justin Jackola</a> and <a href="https://www.elizab
 ethmihelich.com/">Elizabeth Mihelich</a> who joined us for the first time.
 If you missed the event\, you can connect with them via their respective we
 bsites to learn more about what they're up to.</li><li>In the months ahead\
 , we're going to be trying out some different days of the week for these me
 etings. I know of a few folks who are interested in joining but can't do Tu
 esdays\, so we're going to change things up every so often to see if more f
 olks can participate. </li></ul><br>Finally\, mark your calendars for our J
 anuary meeting! On <b>Thursday\, January 18th from 6-8 PM</b>\, you're invi
 ted to Longmont Public Media for a very special session of <b>Stop-Motion M
 ania!!</b> In the span of two hours\, participants will have the chance to
 write\, storyboard\, cast\, and shoot a stop-motion short film. I'll provid
 e prompts\, props\, and set design accoutrements. All you need to do is sho
 w up and be ready to act\, light\, design\, and direct! It'll be a fast and
  fantastic foray into the world of stop-motion!<br><br>I'll send out more i
 nformation as the date gets closer\, but I wanted to let all of you know wh
 at's on the horizon. I might also send out an Eventbrite link so that folks
  can RSVP and I can know how many to expect. Also\, if you aren't doing so
 already\, keep an eye on the Firehouse <a href="https://www.instagram.com/f
 irehouseartcenter/">Instagram </a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/Fi
 rehouseart/">Facebook </a>for updates.<br><br>Hope to see you on Friday\, D
 ecember 8th at Wibby!\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/jhd
 -chdx-uco\nOr dial: (US) +1 540-947-4755 PIN: 625218715#\nMore phone number
 s: https://tel.meet/jhd-chdx-uco?pin=9894937122602&hs=7\n\nLearn more about
  Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
LAST-MODIFIED:20240731T192858Z
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Filmmakers workshop at WIBBY!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20250222T200000Z
DTEND:20250222T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:3u71ntblurf0rf5bds9e0u0sui@google.com
CREATED:20241218T213101Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Sign up <a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-cent
 er-1/schedules/activity-set/1229744">Firehouse Art Center - Paper Pulp Scul
 pting</a></p><p>Paper Making Pulp Sculpting<br>In Pulp Sculpting\, particip
 ants will be using recycled paper and plant pulp to create 3D sculptures fo
 cusing on form and texture. This workshop does not require a particular ski
 ll level\, as we will be playing around with creative new ways to use paper
  pulp other than the traditional pulled sheet method. Participants will lea
 ve with at least one of their own pulp sculptures\, and contribute to a lar
 ger collaborative sculpture that will find a place in the community.<br><br
 >Class fee is $40<br>Maximum of 10 students<br>minimum of 8<br>Any skill le
 vel.<br><br>Meet your instructor- Makenzie Davis<br><br>Makenzie Davis is b
 ased in the Front Range\, living and working between Longmont and Fort Coll
 ins\, CO. Makenzie completed her MFA in Drawing and Painting at the Univers
 ity of Hawaii at Manoa in May 2022. She also holds a BFA in Painting from C
 olorado State University\, where she graduated cum laude in 2017. Makenzie
 currently teaches a range of classes at Front Range Community College\, inc
 luding Drawing I-IV\, Figure Drawing\, 2D Design\, and starting in the Spri
 ng\, Painting I-IV. Alongside teaching\, she works as an Art Director for G
 odot Communications working on projects that span from rebranding town mark
 eting\, creating company logos\, and hosting papermaking workshops that sup
 port the All Nations Support Line across Nebraska. In her personal art prac
 tice\, Makenzie has shown at galleries across the United States with her oi
 l paintings and paper installations that have to do with identity in the sc
 ale of deep time. Recently\, she has shown at the Firehouse Art Center in L
 ongmont\, CO\, where she was also an Artist in Residence for the summer of
 2023. Additionally\, her work has been shown at the Commons Gallery in Oahu
 \, HI\, at Webster Art Center in Webster Groves\, MO\, and at 311 Gallery i
 n Raleigh\, NC.<br><br>Other Things To Know<br><br>Cancellation Policy<br>R
 efund policy: Fees can be refunded with a 48 hour notification before the s
 tart of the first class in a session or 48 hours before the class.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250119T212009Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Paper Sculpting
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
