UID:7vgknjguto9kt9gmf4hg6khp9r@google.com
CREATED:20200822T041541Z
DESCRIPTION:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/spanish-immersion-art-sparks-art-e
 xploration-for-ages-5-7-tickets-116548085461<br><br><p>Our instructor\, Mis
 s Joy\, is a bilingual ELL educator.  She will be teaching each step of the
  project in English first\, then Spanish.  ELL kids will have a chance to s
 pend time hearing and speaking English.  English speaking children will hav
 e exposure to the Spanish language\, strengthening neural pathways that mak
 e language learning easier.  </p><p>10 week session- Art Sparks Spanish Imm
 ersion- Art Exploration classes for ages 5-7</p><p>Consider donating to pro
 vide class supplies for a child in need.  If younger siblings (4 and under
 years of age) are attending\, please purchase a $20 add on per younger chil
 d.</p><p>Zoom format- 1 hour and 15 minutes *last 15 minutes of class is fo
 r art sharing\, and conversing in Spanish and English</p><p>Tuesdays from 9
 am-10:15am</p><p>Supply kit- one time fee of $35</p><p>What instruction wil
 l be offered-</p><p>Weekly there will be a different focus\, fine art/art h
 istory\, math\, science\, and history or social studies.</p><p>Through the
 arts\, we will also include lessons on addition\, subtraction\, patterns\,
 fractions\, animals\, plants\, map making\, cities and towns and more.</p><
 p>Other learning opportunities:</p><p>- Art Theory</p><p>- Color Theory</p>
 <p>- Art terms</p><p>- Care of supplies</p><p>- Kids should be able to work
  independently\, but adults should be nearby in case anything unforeseen ha
 ppens!</p><p>Supply kit lists will be provided\, along with links.  If you
 would like to purchase items on your own\, feel free\, or you can purchase
 as a full kit from the Firehouse .  Supplies will be high quality student g
 rade materials of limited palettes to teach color mixing and blending.</p><
 p>ACCESSIBILITY:</p><p>We are committed to making a space where all childre
 n feel welcome and safe. If there is anything that our educators should kno
 w to ensure your child can access our programming\, please let us know imme
 diately and we will work to provide accommodations.</p><p>TECHNOLOGY:</p><p
 >We will be using Zoom to meet as a group. If you are joining from a comput
 er\, we recommend using a free zoom account join our meeting sessions\, but
  to the best of our knowledge it is not required. </p><p>MEETING LINK</p><p
 >On Monday afternoons\, you will receive an email with information about ac
 cessing our meeting\, any materials you may need\, and a brief overview of
 our plans for Tuesday session. We encourage you to communicate directly wit
 h the educators if you have questions about individual sessions.</p><p>PRIV
 ACY AND SAFETY</p><p>In order to ensure participant privacy and safety\, th
 e Firehouse will take the following steps: </p><p>Participants will always
 be working in groups with other children\, the instructor and an education
 assistant. At no time will participants be alone in a program with other pa
 rticipants or with only one educator.</p><p>Educators will monitor chats an
 d shared camera feed and will take prompt\, appropriate action to curtail i
 nappropriate behavior\, language\, or images. </p><p>The Firehouse will nev
 er record\, screenshot\, or otherwise take images or video of participants.
  </p><p>Please follow the below steps to ensure that your child can be as s
 afe as possible:  </p><p>Please change your screen name to your student's f
 irst name or a preferred nickname--no last names please.</p><p>Please do no
 t share the meeting link with anybody.</p><p>Please set up your student wit
 h a wall behind them to minimize disruptions. Remember that each participan
 t is responsible for what their camera shares with other participants. </p>
 <p>Please do not screenshot or record our meetings.</p><p>VIDEO SHARING AND
  CAMERA ACTIVATION:</p><p>While we encourage participants to activate their
  cameras to enable instructors to provide better instruction\, it is the ca
 regivers choice to do so. By activating your camera\, you give permission f
 or all other participants to see your student and their screen name\, hear
 their voice\, and view their work\, and you grant the Firehouse all necessa
 ry permission to make this content available to other participants. </p><p>
 At the beginning of each session\, we will briefly require each participant
  to turn on their camera so that instructors can confirm (a) that the parti
 cipant is age-appropriate and (b) a caregiver is aware of the child’s parti
 cipation in the program. The caregiver can then turn off their camera if th
 at is more comfortable for them for the remainder of the class.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200822T042340Z
