CREATED:20220125T014736Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>Pine Needle Basket Weaving</b><br>March 19 - noon
  to 3 p.m.<br><br>Use pine needles and waxed linen to weave together basket
 s using our step-by-step instructions/demonstration. Rachel Courtney and Da
 na Steiner will lead the class. All materials will be provided and the clas
 s is $40 at Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue\, Longmont\, CO 80501. RS
 VP at&nbsp\;<a href="http://prettynicecreations.com/event">prettynicecreati
 ons.com/event</a>&nbsp\;to save your seat.<br><br><b>This class repeats on
 April 9</b></html-blob><br><html-blob><b><br></b></html-blob><br><html-blob
 ><b>Bio</b><br>Rachel Courtney has been interested in designing and creatin
 g art from a young age. She has been making hand-made jewelry\, blankets an
 d scarves for decades and recently started painting. She started crocheting
  in 2000 and has been making blankets for Project Linus ever since. She lau
 nched her Etsy store for Pretty Nice Creations in 2010 and has grown her on
 line selling from scarves and blankets to a wide variety of crafts and grap
 hic design work. She enjoys giving crafting classes – alcohol ink\, jewelry
  making\, painting and more.<br><br>Rachel received a bachelor’s degree in
 journalism and mass communications in 2003 and a certificate in digital gra
 phics technology in 2004. Her love of the simple beauties in life led to th
 e founding of her graphic design company\, Pretty Nice Creations where she
 can share her designs with the world. Beyond her graphics and textile work\
 , Rachel is an accomplished photographer and marketing expert who helps loc
 al businesses grow their reach online and off.</html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220306T182515Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pine Needle Basket Weaving with Rachel- Main Gallery
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
