DESCRIPTION:<p>Collagraphs! From collage (you know what that means) and gra
 ph (for print)\, collagraphs can be made from a range of materials with end
 lessly diverse results. In this workshop we'll discuss print design in posi
 tive and negative space\, cut shapes from colorful foam and reassemble/glue
  them on 5x7inch "plates" of cardboard\, then print them with washable wate
 r-based inks.</p><p>Learn about this approachable printing technique and ce
 lebrate St Patrick's Day creatively!</p><p>All supplies and eventbrite fees
  are included\, with 15% of class fees supporting the Firehouse Art Center.
 </p><p>State and County health and safety guidelines will be followed: mask
 s are required.</p><p>This workshop is led by Longmont artist Brandy Coons.
  Coons has curated exhibits at the Firehouse Art Center since 2018\, after
 serving as the Director for ArtWalk Longmont from 2016. She creates drawing
 s\, paintings\, prints\, photographs and objects celebrating the domestic a
 rts\, art history\, and the collector's impulse. You can see more of her wo
 rk on instagram at:</p><p>www.instagram.com/Brandy_Coons</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221220T180741Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Collagraph Workshop with Brandy Coons
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
