CREATED:20241218T203318Z
DESCRIPTION:<h1>Multilayer Monotype Class</h1><br>Sign up here: <a href="ht
 tps://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/122974
 5">Firehouse Art Center - Multilayer Monotype Class</a><br><br><p>Multilaye
 r Monotype Class</p><p>We will learn about the versatile printmaking method
  of monotype! This particular approach will use plexiglass and additive/sub
 tractive ways of applying ink. Students will leave with around 5 unique pri
 nts.</p><p>Age range: 14 and up (under 18 accompanied by a guardian)</p><p>
 Min Students: 4</p><p>Max Students: 10</p><p>Class fee: $25</p><p>Meet your
  Instructor: Andi Newberry</p><p>Andi Newberry (she/her) is a printmaker an
 d multi-disciplinary artist whose work often explores the impermanence of h
 er memories and connections with others. She was born in Wichita Falls\, Te
 xas. She graduated with an MFA from the University of Colorado\, Boulder an
 d earned her BFA from Midwestern State University. Andi has organized and p
 articipated in many printmaking portfolio exchanges\, connecting her with a
 rtists from all over the world. Her print and multi-media textile works hav
 e been accepted to exhibitions for PrintAustin\, PrintHouston\, and Denver’
 s Month of Printmaking at the Arvada Center and ArtGym in Denver. She relis
 hes teaching\, sharing the experience of creating prints\, and connecting w
 ith others in the studio—endlessly falling in love with printmaking all ove
 r again.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250119T212801Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Multilayer Monotype Printmaking with Andi
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
