CREATED:20200822T054209Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Saturday: 12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (open to walk in guests with a
 5 person capacity)<br></p><p>The Firehouse is so excited to be opening for
 weekday appointments\, and with a 5 person capacity on Saturdays. I have be
 en receiving questions regarding safety and what to expect at the gallery (
 from staff as well as the community) as we reopen. Sorry for the long post
 in advance.<br></p><p>Appointments- Sunday and Wednesday through Friday\, g
 uests can request a time to visit between 12pm and 5pm.&nbsp\; Appointments
  can be made by emailing info@firehouseart.org.&nbsp\; Someone will email b
 ack confirming your time slot as well as safety procedures.</p><p>Saturday
 – There is a 5 person limit in the gallery. You will be allowed to enter be
 tween 12pm-5pm as capacity permits.</p><p>We are so excited to share these
 works with you\, and we have implemented some safety precautions to keep ou
 r community safe as well as prevent the spread of COVID-19. We ask that if
 you are exhibiting any symptoms of COVID-19 (fever\, cough\, shortness of b
 reath) that you stay home except to seek medical help.</p><p>1. Deep clean-
  The Firehouse was deep cleaned before reopening.</p><p>2. Masks- All guest
 s must follow mandatory state requirements for masks. If you do not have a
 mask\, they are available at the Firehouse for a $5 donation. We will not b
 e allowing guests to enter without a mask\, so please be prepared.<br>Your
 cloth face covering should:<br>Reach above the nose\, below the chin\, and
 completely cover the mouth and nostrils<br>Fit snugly against the sides of
 the face<br>Be made of multiple layers of fabric that you can still breathe
  through<br>Be able to be laundered and machine dried without damaging the
 material or shape<br>Learn more at&nbsp\;<a href="https://l.facebook.com/l.
 php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fbit.ly%2F2Ravt42%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR0ZLNqI2f4fGXZGIw3O4RQqO
 pkcKPWE5BByKMdLRliBv2oELZ24McC_4VI&amp\;h=AT1dbZa4ScpJou1nVrlsRDfPz4UE_h1QS
 WHuaZo5i4nh9bHRdEPjXQfizhiS69d2aqVt5GBmdWGmTBF9Wmn-cLRhEssG8h5sP8-Qv0IOWwYE
 ehBOY3cXcnd06XhgiJavcFxdSfSxt79ro-9FBnVGjhbBdfGkJrsh8IFB2ACGgZggn0N-58_L3q5
 UkL5pJn6woKCkN6pl8Hws8yXnVyI_4vm34WISSc40Vej17fWRTM6YRPma9GPMHZPwPcVhOzEGao
 0yX7YQLpHtNK1sA1U-lC6ig5OyY9OaU6NCtBZMJFNx8-h5V53Docj5OZGlGr_cIyo9HI-YeMQY8
 -3yW21f13HlFUWnsauITdj0h9lp2lebi688MdBPSf3NizG90KHZmqjAg4X6hLLVEtzdzwGew0ox
 lhWLEPFSul8KllW1c2EIVqDrLSk8uYVXVQvbkr5sUFp8YUvgdbva-F-5BNQNCWb7f7yEbgwySdv
 YkCNRAw9tJvEhV-w3Pf9BXOqQJbQ4AsYrYznFNtnl5Im4auLUlAsMLNKrFh-VCDCrtMnrsn6Jv2
 DL6Ef7-1OO8owIIAXWPkH_lsSOSXnWqZsPD5TuxpC9tfgAZHvwXAm1dzDDA8CVU3Wq4o8Nlv4vw
 HbjzxnkJQ">https://bit.ly/2Ravt42</a></p><p>3. Viewing and learning about t
 he artwork- Please follow the directional arrows for viewing the artwork.</
 p><p>4. Please keep staff and volunteers in mind- If you have questions abo
 ut the gallery or the artwork\, we welcome them! Please feel free to ask qu
 estions at an appropriate six foot distance to protect our staff and volunt
 eers.</p><p>5. What we are doing to keep you safe- Staff and volunteers wil
 l wear masks during appointments/weekend open times\, as well as sterilize
 surfaces and wash hands after every appointment/every 30 minutes. Antibacte
 rial gel is available to guests at different stations throughout the galler
 y.</p><p>We are excited for you to come see the show and we appreciate your
  cooperation on our new policies as we move forward with reopening!<br>– El
 aine Waterman<br></p><p>Executive Director</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20210213T223221Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Gallery open to walk ins
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
