DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://firehouseart.org/summeronthestreets/">Summer o
 n the Streets 2023 - Firehouse Art Center</a> <br><br>Summer on the Streets
 : Papermaking Workshops - July 8th\, August 12th<br>These community based p
 apermaking workshops will explore the landscape of Longmont by means of two
  papermaking methods: the pulled sheet and the poured sheet. Participants w
 ill be using paper pulp collected from the community to pull their own uniq
 ue sheets of paper in a more traditional method\, adding paint\, natural pi
 gments\, and plants as part of the process. Additionally\, participants wil
 l work together on a large\, collaborative sheet of poured paper that will
 be integrated into Makenzie’s final exhibition at the Firehouse Art Center’
 s Main Gallery in September.<br><br>Materials that the community can contri
 bute before the workshop include:<br>- Newspaper<br>- Junk mail<br>- Scrap
 paper (from notebooks\, sticky notes\, etc.)<br>- Any paper detritus that w
 ould otherwise be thrown away<br><br>It’s helpful if this paper is shredded
  or torn up into smaller pieces when delivered to the Firehouse\, but it do
 es not need to be (there will be additional events that focus on just prepa
 ring the paper for pulp and sharing stories). Regardless of how the paper i
 s donated\, it will be ready for use in the workshops\, where participants
 will explore the versatile nature of papermaking as well as a way to connec
 t and build community.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230607T234738Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Summer on the Streets- Makenzie Davis Papermaking workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
