DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><h1><strong style="font-size: 14px\;">MARCH 3
 \, 10\, 17\, 24</strong><br></h1><h1><p><span style="font-weight: normal\;"
 ><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/tweenteen-drawing-class-ages-10-15-t
 hursdays-at-415-tickets-264558580837" id="ow3644" __is_owner="true">SIGN UP
 - $44 first child\, $35 second child</a><br>4 WEEK SESSION</span></p><p><sp
 an style="font-weight: normal\;">Designed for ages 10-15\, teen classes enc
 ourage young artists to experiment and develop their own personal style.</s
 pan></p><p><span style="font-weight: normal\;">This weekly 75-minute class
 is for students who Want to learn drawing skills as a foundation for other
 arts. We will have a different project each week.</span></p><p><span style=
 "font-weight: normal\;">Week 1- Still life and drawing from observation<br>
 Week 2- White and Color on black paper<br>Week 3- Grid drawings<br>Week 4-
 Personal style drawings- bring sketchbooks!</span></p><p><span style="font-
 weight: normal\;">Projects will include working with still life\, breaking
 down a photograph\, portrait work\, developing illustration skills and more
 . All supplies are included and will vary within projects. Supplies may inc
 lude pastel\, marker\, colored pencil\, ink and charcoal pencils.&nbsp\;Ple
 ase bring any samples you may have of past student work on the first day so
  class so that the instructor may gauge the student's learning level\, and
 discuss possible projects and goals with the student. </span></p><p><span s
 tyle="font-weight: normal\;">- Kids should be able to work independently</s
 pan></p></h1><u></u></html-blob>
