DESCRIPTION:<p>Sign up here: <a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/firehous
 e-makes-a-movie-tickets-836713822567">https://www.eventbrite.com/e/firehous
 e-makes-a-movie-tickets-836713822567</a></p><p><span><br></span></p><p><spa
 n>You\, the members of Firehouse\, are invited to an evening of relaxing cr
 eative playtime as we practice the tactile methods of experimental cinema.
 In other words\, you're invited to color on 16mm film using the supplies th
 at Allison will provide. As you are coloring and painting\, your host\, All
 ison\, will document the experience on Super 8 film. At the end of the nigh
 t\, Allison will get all of the footage digitized and edit it together so t
 hat you can see the fruits of your artistic play come together into a finis
 hed short film.</span></p><p></p><p>We'll begin the night with a brief scre
 ening of a few short films by Stan Brakhage\, one of most important names i
 n experimental cinema who also happened to call Boulder\, Colorado his home
  for much of his career. After this inspiration\, Allison will give you a q
 uick tutorial in basic practices for painting on and distorting your film.
 Then\, you can spend the rest of the evening going bonkers on your section
 of film.</p><p></p><p>Never heard of Stan Brakhage? Never made a movie\, or
  even picked up a paintbrush? That's okay! Playing with the medium and lear
 ning about it as you create is what experimental cinema is all about.</p><p
 ></p><p>Finally\, just a note for all participants: You will be supplied wi
 th paint\, nail polish\, markers\, and sculpting tools which you can use to
  color\, scratch\, and distort your film. Allison will provide gloves. Just
  to be on the extra safe side\, I recommend wearing casual clothes that can
  withstand the chance of paint splatter.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240212T221347Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Main Gallery- Filmmaker Social- PAinted film- Allison- radomskialli
 son@gmail.com
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
