DESCRIPTION:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/spanish-immersion-in-person-and-zo
 om-open-age-range-up-to-12-tickets-116684930769<br><br><p>Our instructor\,
 Miss Joy\, is a bilingual ELL educator.  She will be teaching each step of
 the project in English first\, then Spanish.  ELL kids will have a chance t
 o spend time hearing and speaking English.  English speaking children will
 have exposure to the Spanish language\, strengthening neural pathways that
 make language learning easier.   This class is in person and limited to 6 k
 ids\, Zoom is limited to 10 kids</p><p>10 week session</p><p>Consider donat
 ing $65 to provide classes for a child in need and increase enrollment by o
 ne\, dropping your price as well.  </p><p>For questions about pricing and s
 cholarships\, please  email info@firehouseart.org.  We would love to be abl
 e to support arts education for all and for $65\, one child in need will be
  able to attend 10 classes for free.  </p><p>In person format- 1 hour and 1
 5 minutes *last 15 minutes of class is for art sharing\, and conversing in
 Spanish and English</p><p>Zoom format is real time as in person and will no
 t be recorded.</p><p>Mondays at 9am-10:15am</p><p>Supply kit- one time fee
 of $35</p><p>What instruction will be offered-</p><p>- Art Theory</p><p>- C
 olor Theory</p><p>- Art terms</p><p>- Care of supplies</p><p>- Kids should
 be able to work independently\, but adults should be nearby in case anythin
 g unforeseen happens!</p><p>Supply kit lists will be provided\, along with
 links.  If you would like to purchase items on your own\, feel free\, or yo
 u can purchase as a full kit from the Firehouse .  Supplies will be high qu
 ality student grade materials of limited palettes to teach color mixing and
  blending.</p><p>SCHOLARSHIPS \, IN PERSON AND DONATION BASED CLASSES:</p><
 p>These are awarded on a case by case basis.  Please contact info@firehouse
 art.org to inquire about qualifications.  Applications must be filled out a
 nd approved before choosing the pay what you can based fee structure.  We w
 ill also be working with SVVSD to identify ELL children and children in nee
 d.</p><p>ACCESSIBILITY:</p><p>We are committed to making a space where all
 children feel welcome and safe. If there is anything that our educators sho
 uld know to ensure your child can access our programming\, please let us kn
 ow immediately and we will work to provide accommodations.</p><p>TECHNOLOGY
 :</p><p>We will be using Zoom to meet as a group. If you are joining from a
  computer\, we recommend using a free zoom account join our meeting session
 s\, but to the best of our knowledge it is not required.</p><p>MEETING LINK
 </p><p>On Firday afternoons\, you will receive an email with information ab
 out accessing our meeting\, any materials you may need\, and a brief overvi
 ew of our plans for Monday's session. We encourage you to communicate direc
 tly with the educators if you have questions about individual sessions.</p>
 <p>PRIVACY AND SAFETY</p><p>In order to ensure participant privacy and safe
 ty\, the Firehouse will take the following steps:</p><p>Participants will a
 lways be working in groups with other children\, the instructor and an educ
 ation assistant. At no time will participants be alone in a program with ot
 her participants or with only one educator.</p><p>Educators will monitor ch
 ats and shared camera feed and will take prompt\, appropriate action to cur
 tail inappropriate behavior\, language\, or images.</p><p>The Firehouse wil
 l never record\, screenshot\, or otherwise take images or video of particip
 ants.</p><p></p><p>Please follow the below steps to ensure that your child
 can be as safe as possible:</p><p></p><p>Please change your screen name to
 your student's first name or a preferred nickname--no last names please.</p
 ><p></p><p>Please do not share the meeting link with anybody.</p><p></p><p>
 Please set up your student with a wall behind them to minimize disruptions.
  Remember that each participant is responsible for what their camera shares
  with other participants.</p><p></p><p>Please do not screenshot or record o
 ur meetings.</p><p></p><p>VIDEO SHARING AND CAMERA ACTIVATION:</p><p></p><p
 >While we encourage participants to activate their cameras to enable instru
 ctors to provide better instruction\, it is the caregivers choice to do so.
  By activating your camera\, you give permission for all other participants
  to see your student and their screen name\, hear their voice\, and view th
 eir work\, and you grant the Firehouse all necessary permission to make thi
 s content available to other participants.</p><p></p><p>At the beginning of
  each session\, we will briefly require each participant to turn on their c
 amera so that instructors can confirm (a) that the participant is age-appro
 priate and (b) a caregiver is aware of the child’s participation in the pro
 gram. The caregiver can then turn off their camera if that is more comforta
 ble for them for the remainder of the class.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p><p></p><p></p
 >
