DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/diy-film-processing-night
 -tickets-951653750987?utm-campaign=social&amp\;utm-content=attendeeshare&am
 p\;utm-medium=discovery&amp\;utm-term=listing&amp\;utm-source=cp&amp\;aff=e
 bdsshcopyurl">DIY Film Processing Night Tickets\, Thu\, Aug 15\, 2024 at 6:
 00 PM | Eventbrite</a><br><br><p>On <strong><b><strong><b>Thursday\, August
  15th</b></strong></b></strong>\, join Firehouse Filmmakers at <strong><b><
 strong><b>Firehouse Art Center</b></strong></b></strong> for our first-ever
  <strong><b><strong><b>DIY Film Processing Night</b></strong></b></strong>!
  In this session\, we’ll be developing our own rolls of 35mm film and creat
 ing digital scans of the results. If you’ve always wanted to learn how to d
 evelop your own film (or\, if you’ve just been looking for an appropriate s
 pace to use film processing chemicals)\, please join us! Please register he
 re so that we can know how many folks to expect.</p><p><em><strong><b><stro
 ng><b>A quick note about this event:</b></strong></b></strong></em> the DIY
  Film Processing Night is following up on the Still Photography Film Hack\,
  where participants learned how to make their own still photography film ro
 lls using motion picture film (spoiler alert: it’s super easy to do and way
  cheaper than purchasing still photography rolls). Since those rolls were m
 ade with ECN2 film\, we’ll be using ECN2 chemistry to develop those rolls.
 If you did not attend this event and you have a different film roll that yo
 u’d like to develop\, you’re still welcome to join this event and participa
 te. Just know that processing your roll in a different type of chemistry wi
 ll alter your images and colors. But\, if you’re game for the gamble of cro
 ss-processing (which is super fun and I hope you’ll give it a try!)\, pleas
 e join us. All equipment and chemicals will be provided. <strong><b><strong
 ><b>All you need to bring is one roll of 35mm film to develop.</b></strong>
 </b></strong></p>
