DESCRIPTION:<p>The Dia de los Muertos Family Fiesta and the Catrina Ball wi
 ll be here soon!</p><p><span>Join Meow Wolf at the Firehouse and make marig
 old and butterfly masks and headpieces to get you ready for the ball!</span
 ></p><p><span>Kate Major\, professional costume and creature maker at Denve
 r’s Convergence Station\, will be inside the Firehouse&#39\;s Main and Sout
 h Gallery for an all-ages building workshop. Come make a mask or headpiece
 to wear to the Gigantes Procession on October 14th. </span></p><p><span>Mat
 erials will include recylced items\, flowers\, and paper mache. These will
 be privided along with c</span><span>ardboard\, bubble wrap\, packing mater
 ials\, yarn\, pipe cleaners\, paint and glue. We encourage you to bring you
 r own materials to build with too! Please leave glass\, sharp metal\, anyth
 ing dirty\, wet\, icky or gross at home\, though.</span></p><p>Tickets are
 $7 per person and kids under 12 are free (please have 1 adult for every 2 k
 ids under 12). Proceeds will help support the Firehouse Art Center.<br></p>
