DESCRIPTION:<p>Join Ana Balzan in this fun mask making workshop.</p><p>Ana
 will help students in...</p><p>• The skull basics - checking height\, width
  &amp\; length of the head with the help of a generic proportions calculato
 r.</p><p>• Using additive processes to create realistic features and bone s
 tructure while applying face proportions learned.</p><p>• Adding masses and
  developing the primary features: nose\, lips and eyeballs.</p><p>• Gradual
  detailing\, fussing and checking symmetry</p><p>• Creating a human mask wi
 th Ana’s assistance making features of their choosing.</p><p>• Ana will pro
 vide 3 female face images.</p><p>• Creating slip to join clay pieces togeth
 er.</p><p>• Clean surface with scrubby pad and terry cloth</p><p>• Learning
  to refine and re-shape the features to create their vision with as much or
  little realism as desired.</p><p>• Form holes to enable the mask to be dis
 played on a wall with string or wire.</p><p>The masks will be fired (bisque
  firing is included in the price) and students will be able to pick up 2 we
 eks after the class. They can then be taken home to paint\, or can be glaze
 d at the Firehouse and refired for $15.</p><p><br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240111T173627Z
LOCATION:Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue\, Longmont\, CO 80501
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Clay Mask Making Workshop with Ana Balzan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
