CREATED:20230921T161620Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/closing-reception-arti
 st-talk-makenzie-davis-lignin-a-homecoming-tickets-723467108597?aff=oddtdtc
 reator"><u>Closing Reception &amp\; Artist Talk: Makenzie Davis- "Lignin: A
  Homecoming" Tickets\, Sun\, Oct 8\, 2023 at 10:00 AM | Eventbrite</u></a><
 br></p><p><strong><b><br></b></strong></p><p><strong><b>Closing Reception &
 amp\; Artist Talk: Makenzie Davis- "Lignin: A Homecoming"</b></strong></p><
 p>Join us for a special closing reception and artist talk with Makenzie Dav
 is as she takes us on a journey through her captivating exhibition\, Lignin
 : A Homecoming. Get ready to gain a deeper understanding of her creative pr
 ocess and to be immersed in her residency installation and place based pape
 r making work. Learn about how\, through the paper making process\, she was
  able to reconnect with her home and her community\,</p><p>Join us in perso
 n or virtually as we engage in a lively conversation about Lignin through t
 his unique opportunity to connect with Makenzie Davis and explore the stori
 es behind the paper.</p><p>Q&amp\;A and a final artist walkthrough of the e
 xhibit will occur after the talk. Makenzie is inviting all community paper
 makers who were included in the exhibit to come retrieve their work and sha
 re any stories about their creation. Makeznie will also be gifting communit
 y paper made paper pieces to guests\, so make sure to attend to take a piec
 e of paper art home with you!</p><p><strong><b>About the exhibit and the ar
 tist</b></strong></p><p>In Lignin: A Homecoming\, Davis facilitates social
 ties and material connections\, comparing Longmont’s inhabitants to the nat
 ural world\, namely\, the omnipresent element of lignin. Lignin is a class
 of complex organic polymers that form key structural materials and supporti
 ve tissues of most plants. Integral to the structure of Longmont and the ex
 hibit itself is the similarly supporting role of the community.</p><p>After
  completing her three year Master of Fine Arts degree at the University of
 Hawaii\, Davis returned to Longmont in May of 2022. The Firehouse residency
  offered a way to reconnect to her art practice outside of academia and obs
 erve changes in the local landscape. During the two month residency\, she e
 xpanded upon her painting and paper-making practices by taking a deeper loo
 k into the transforming environment of her home in the Front Range. Expansi
 ve oil paintings depict the familiar and iconic landscapes of Longmont\, wh
 ile handmade paper displays the more abstract components of the local lands
 cape such as organic materials\, natural processes\, and the lignin-like co
 mmunity members: people who act as the fibers that form and support our cul
 ture. Longmont residents were initially invited to participate by donating
 junk mail and newspapers. Additionally\, various plant matter and soil were
  sourced from all over town and the surrounding areas. Most of the handmade
  paper in the exhibit was created in collaboration with those who participa
 ted in her papermaking workshops. By layering this material over areas of t
 he paintings\, Davis reveals the truest landscape of Longmont – the tightly
  woven lignin of its community.</p><p><strong><b>About the Residency Progra
 m</b></strong></p><p>The Firehouse Art Center hosts two residencies each ye
 ar\, working in the South Gallery for three months before a culminating sol
 o exhibition in the Main Gallery with the opportunity to guest curate the a
 ccompanying South Gallery.</p><p>The Artist Occupied program at the Firehou
 se Art Center is intended as a professional development opportunity for eme
 rging and experienced visual artists.Bring you work to a new creative level
  as you connect visitors to working artist environments and processes.</p><
 p>Previous resident artists include Heather Kegel\, Sean Faling\, Jessica F
 orrestal\, Chris Blume\, Kaitlyn Tucek\, Roberta Restaino\, Chelsea Gilmore
 \, Barbara Rudlaff\, Amy Hoagland\, Janelle Anderson\, Jono Wright\, and Na
 ncy Eastman.</p><p><strong><b>Support the Firehouse</b></strong></p><p>If y
 ou’re feeling inspired to support our resident artists\, their projects\, o
 r the Firehouse Art Center\, please visit <a href="https://firehouseart.org
 /donate">https://firehouseart.org/donate</a> and give today by becoming a m
 onthly supporter or by making a one-time donation. Thank you!<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230921T161657Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Closing Reception & Artist Talk: Makenzie Davis- "Lignin: A Homecom
 ing"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
