CREATED:20211127T201949Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><b>Lino Block Printing<br></b><br>Saturday\, Feb. 5 - noon
 to 3 p.m.<br>Join Rachel Courtney and Dana Steiner for a block painting cla
 ss. Use blocks\, cutters and brayers to create a reusable relief print of y
 our own creation. All materials will be provided and the class is $40 at Fi
 rehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Avenue\, Longmont\, CO 80501.&nbsp\;RSVP at&nb
 sp\;<a href="http://prettynicecreations.com/event">prettynicecreations.com/
 event</a>. Students will have the opportunity to make 2 designs on 4x6 lino
 . Bring any sketches you may need to complete them\, they can be cut into s
 maller sizes\, you can draw straight on to the lino\, or free cut the desig
 ns.<br><br><b>Needle Felted Goats Milk Soap Workshop</b><br>Saturday\, Feb.
  26 - noon to 3 p.m.<br>Felted soaps are a functional soap with an artistic
  scrubby built in! When your soap is spent you will be left with a little w
 ool felted pouch that you can poke a hole in and add new soap\, use it to h
 old potpourri\, air plants or coins. This class is geared towards beginners
  but fun for felters of any experience level. This class includes an unscen
 ted goats milk soap\, wool and tools to complete a single felted soap. All
 materials will be provided and the class is $40 at Firehouse Art Center\, 6
 67 4th Avenue\, Longmont\, CO 80501. RSVP at&nbsp\;<a href="http://prettyni
 cecreations.com/event">prettynicecreations.com/event</a>&nbsp\;to save your
  seat.<br><br><b>Bio</b><br>Rachel Courtney has been interested in designin
 g and creating art from a young age. She has been making hand-made jewelry\
 , blankets and scarves for decades and recently started painting. She start
 ed crocheting in 2000 and has been making blankets for Project Linus ever s
 ince. She launched her Etsy store for Pretty Nice Creations in 2010 and has
  grown her online selling from scarves and blankets to a wide variety of cr
 afts and graphic design work. She enjoys giving crafting classes – alcohol
 ink\, jewelry making\, painting and more.<br><br>Rachel received a bachelor
 ’s degree in journalism and mass communications in 2003 and a certificate i
 n digital graphics technology in 2004. Her love of the simple beauties in l
 ife led to the founding of her graphic design company\, Pretty Nice Creatio
 ns where she can share her designs with the world. Beyond her graphics and
 textile work\, Rachel is an accomplished photographer and marketing expert
 who helps local businesses grow their reach online and off.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221220T180722Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Lino Block Printing with Rachel
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
