DESCRIPTION:POSTPONED DUE TO weather!\n\nHi Everyone\,\n\nIt's kind of rain
 y and windy and moths don't like that weather! So we're going to reschedule
  for August!\n\nStay tuned for the rescheduled date and sorry for the late
 cancellation!\n\nBest\,\n\nErica\nRegister here- https://www.eventbrite.com
 /e/956739572817  or just stop on by!\nMoths are crucial pollinators that ar
 e often overlooked. Because they are largely nocturnal\, many people are le
 ss familiar with moths than they are with butterflies. Amazingly\, there ar
 e over 160\,000 known species of moths in the world\, compared to less than
  18\,000 species of butterflies. In tandem with National Moth Week\, and in
  an effort to shed light on the local Lepidoptera kingdom\, summer artist-i
 n-residence Erica Podwoiski invites you to her studio for a Midsummer Night
 ’s Mothball!\nThis indoor/outdoor nighttime event welcomes curious folks of
  all ages to gather\, appreciate\, and observe moths. From 8-10 PM\, Erica
 will share her artwork and documentation of her own moth findings in the st
 udio while a moth-ing station will attract moths outside. Acting as citizen
  scientists\, visitors will be encouraged to document their findings and sh
 are their images with Scientific databases like iNaturalist.\nHeadlamps and
  flashlights are strongly encouraged\, along with a desire to become a moth
 -er!\nErica will have a simple observation station around the corner from h
 er South Gallery Studio. It will be located in the lot directly South of th
 e Firehouse. There will be lights aimed directly at the wall and hopefully
 we will be able to attract some moths!\nThis is a precursor event to Erica'
 s larger moth-ing event at Sunflower Farm!
LAST-MODIFIED:20240726T205539Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Postponed!  Midsummer MothBall
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
