UID:01l1mjmgkhqrjbf5ck34p7cmsf@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Denver:20200908T113000
CREATED:20200822T041204Z
DESCRIPTION:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/art-sparks-art-exploration-for-age
 s-5-7-zoom-class-tickets-116542815699<br><br><p>10 week session- Art Sparks
 - Art Exploration classes for ages 5-7</p><p>Consider donating $65 to provi
 de classes for a child in need and increase enrollment by one\, dropping yo
 ur price as well.  If younger siblings (under 5) are attending\, please pur
 chase a $20 add on per younger child.</p><p>For questions about pricing and
  scholarships\, please  email info@firehouseart.org.  We would love to be a
 ble to support arts education for all and for $65\, one child in need will
 be able to attend 10 classes for free.  </p><p>Zoom format- 1 hour and 15 m
 inutes *last 15 minutes of class is for art sharing</p><p>Tuesday at 11:30a
 m-12:45pm</p><p>Supply kit- $35\, or $50 for a shared kit for 2 siblings</p
 ><p>What instruction will be offered-</p><p>Weekly there will be a differen
 t focus\, fine art/art history\, math\, science\, and history or social stu
 dies.</p><p>Through the arts\, we will also include lessons on addition\, s
 ubtraction\, patterns\, fractions\, animals\, plants\, map making\, cities
 and towns and more.</p><p>Other learning opportunities:</p><p>- Art Theory<
 /p><p>- Color Theory</p><p>- Art terms</p><p>- Care of supplies</p><p>- Kid
 s should be able to work independently\, but adults should be nearby in cas
 e anything unforeseen happens!</p><p>Supply kit lists will be provided\, al
 ong with links.  If you would like to purchase items on your own\, feel fre
 e\, or you can purchase as a full kit from the Firehouse .  Supplies will b
 e high quality student grade materials of limited palettes to teach color m
 ixing and blending.</p><p>ACCESSIBILITY:</p><p>We are committed to making a
  space where all children feel welcome and safe. If there is anything that
 our educators should know to ensure your child can access our programming\,
  please let us know immediately and we will work to provide accommodations.
 </p><p>TECHNOLOGY:</p><p>We will be using Zoom to meet as a group. If you a
 re joining from a computer\, we recommend using a free zoom account join ou
 r meeting sessions\, but to the best of our knowledge it is not required. <
 /p><p>MEETING LINK</p><p>On Monday afternoons\, you will receive an email w
 ith information about accessing our meeting\, any materials you may need\,
 and a brief overview of our plans for Tuesday's session. We encourage you t
 o communicate directly with the educators if you have questions about indiv
 idual sessions.</p><p>PRIVACY AND SAFETY</p><p>In order to ensure participa
 nt privacy and safety\, the Firehouse will take the following steps: </p><p
 >Participants will always be working in groups with other children\, the in
 structor and an education assistant. At no time will participants be alone
 in a program with other participants or with only one educator.</p><p>Educa
 tors will monitor chats and shared camera feed and will take prompt\, appro
 priate action to curtail inappropriate behavior\, language\, or images. </p
 ><p>The Firehouse will never record\, screenshot\, or otherwise take images
  or video of participants. </p><p>Please follow the below steps to ensure t
 hat your child can be as safe as possible:  </p><p>Please change your scree
 n name to your student's first name or a preferred nickname--no last names
 please.</p><p>Please do not share the meeting link with anybody.</p><p>Plea
 se set up your student with a wall behind them to minimize disruptions. Rem
 ember that each participant is responsible for what their camera shares wit
 h other participants. </p><p>Please do not screenshot or record our meeting
 s.</p><p>VIDEO SHARING AND CAMERA ACTIVATION:</p><p>While we encourage part
 icipants to activate their cameras to enable instructors to provide better
 instruction\, it is the caregivers choice to do so. By activating your came
 ra\, you give permission for all other participants to see your student and
  their screen name\, hear their voice\, and view their work\, and you grant
  the Firehouse all necessary permission to make this content available to o
 ther participants. </p><p>At the beginning of each session\, we will briefl
 y require each participant to turn on their camera so that instructors can
 confirm (a) that the participant is age-appropriate and (b) a caregiver is
 aware of the child’s participation in the program. The caregiver can then t
 urn off their camera if that is more comfortable for them for the remainder
  of the class</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200822T042347Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Zoom- Art Sparks- Art Exploration classes for ages 5-7
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
