UID:3lko9tvqk9q1uoopka7jhhrbp4@google.com
CREATED:20190729T182046Z
DESCRIPTION:Many More Tomorrow’s – September Suicide Prevention<br>2nd  wee
 k ART Schedule<br><br><b>Monday 9/9 :  Grey Havens -  Art project &amp\; di
 scussion </b><br>Firehouse  Art Center  <br><br><b>Tuesday 9/10:  Kindness
 Rocks – Senior Center 9 am – 10am</b><br>Christine Saunders \, Life Coach o
 f WholeHearted Life Coaching – facilitator<br>Our Kindness Rocks project go
 al is simple... to promote random acts of kindness to unsuspecting recipien
 ts by painting and dropping inspirational rocks around our community.<br>Th
 ese rocks are for anyone who needs them. Take them\, leave them\, photograp
 h them\, or share them with someone who needs a little kindness and love.<b
 r>Supplies will be provided.  We encourage you to Bring Your Own Rock “BYOR
 ” (we will have some there if you forget ????)<br>Connect with friends and
 your community for this fun filled morning of promoting and sharing kindnes
 s.<br><br><b>Encouragement Board -  Firehouse  Art Center  3-5 p</b> – Paul
 a Peacock – facilitator<br>Need a lift me up? During September\,  Suicide P
 revention month you can stop by the Firehouse Art Center and pick up letter
 s of encouragement and positivity. Take one and leave a preprinted one for
 the next person or write your own note to leave for the next person who nee
 ds encouragement. The encouragement board will be available beginning Tuesd
 ay Sept. 10 at the Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Ave.<br><br><b>Wednesday
 9/11:  3p – 5p  OUR Center - Soft Voices </b><br><br>Celebration of Ryan Sp
 ickard’s Life –local artist &amp\; Soft Voices Member-  with Cornelia Spick
 ard . Poetry and Contemplation– Stephanie Pache\, facilitator <br>Imagine a
  brief pause in your day.  Time to soak in the words of poetry.  Share in t
 he company of listening ears &amp\; open hearts. Come and welcome the langu
 age of poetry into your life. Poetry and contemplative reading practices ar
 e tools for reflecting and connecting more deeply with our own inner wisdom
 . We will read and listen to poems\, journal\, and share our individual res
 ponses.<br>No prior experience with poetry or contemplative reading practic
 es necessary!<br><br><b>Thursday 9/12 : Vision Board –  Recovery Café – 6p
 -7:30p  </b> <br>Christine Saunders\, Life Coach of Wholehearted Life Coach
 ing - facilitator<br>Vision Boards – one of the most valuable tools for sel
 f expression\, a way create a tangible example\, idea or expression of your
  future tomorrows.  It can represent your goals\, dreams and ideal life.  C
 reate &amp\; imagine a bright vision of your many tomorrows using collages
 &amp\; visioning techniques.  Supplies provided.<br><br><b>Friday  9/13 : C
 ommunity Memory Weaving–  2nd Friday  Firehouse Art Center 6- 9p</b><br><b>
  Paula Peacock - facilitator</b><br>We are all connected in the warp and we
 ft of life. Participate in a Community Memory Weaving by Celebrating someon
 e you know who has committed suicide or seriously considered it. Strips of
 fabric will be supplied to use to hold  your loved ones’ name in the Weavin
 g.  Stop by the Firehouse Art Center\,  667 4th Ave.\, Sept. 10 between 3 -
 5pm to add the name of  a loved one to the Community&#39\;s Collaborative
 Memory Weaving Project.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190729T182046Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Many More Tomorrow’s – September Suicide Prevention 2nd week ART Sc
 hedule
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
