DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:s03s12p1vntqgdk2ubm4c78p0k@google.com
CREATED:20241218T193549Z
DESCRIPTION:More info and rsvp here- <a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/fire
 house-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1219034">Firehouse Art Center - L
 earn to Crochet</a><br><br>Class Experience<br>This class is perfect for to
 tal beginners wanting to get started on their crochet journey. You'll learn
  how to hold the hook and yarn\, and complete basic crochet stitches.<br><b
 r>Class fee: $20 per person (each attendee will be given yarn\, hook\, and
 handout to take home).<br><br>Ages 16+<br><br>Maximum class size of 10 peop
 le.<br><br>Offering the same class every month on the second Monday of the
 month from January 13- May 12<br><br>Meet your instructor: Amber Ivey<br><b
 r>Although Amber Ivey is technically an artistic dabbler\, enjoying a varie
 ty of arts and crafts\, she has been crocheting for over 10 years\, and has
  a plethora of crochet teaching experience thanks to running the Longmont C
 ommunity Crochet Guild since 2018. Prior to running the guild\, she was a f
 ull time mom\, and prior to becoming a mom she worked as a middle school ma
 th teacher. Her past interests have seen her try pottery\, acting\, furnitu
 re refinishing\, poetry writing\, black and white photography\, bookbinding
 \, ballroom dancing\, upholstery\, jewelry making\, sewing\, embroidery\, c
 ollage\, graphic design\, and knitting. She has lived in Miami\, NYC\, and
 France\, and dreams of one day being fluent in Spanish and visiting Cuba.<b
 r><br>What To Bring<br>each attendee will be given yarn\, hook\, and handou
 t to take home<br>You don't NEED to bring any supplies\, but if you have ya
 rn and/or hooks already\, you can bring them and we can discuss whether or
 not they are good for beginners.<br>It would also be great to know ahead of
  time if folks are *right* handed or *left* handed!!
LAST-MODIFIED:20250119T204509Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learn to crochet
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
