DTSTART:20210624T160000Z
DTEND:20210624T191500Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:4p1ekqp30clbtqgs3ms5hqtk2u@google.com
CREATED:20210525T010203Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><br><br><strong>Mix and match your collage materials with o
 ther participants in advance of this online group workshop taught by artist
  Janelle W Anderson</strong><br><strong><br></strong><br><strong>More info
 here- https://www.eventbrite.com/e/155818714971</strong><br><br><h2>About t
 his event</h2><br><br><p>Join us for a unique and socially distanced collag
 e workshop!</p><p>Firehouse Art Center summer 2021 Artist-In-Residence Jane
 lle W Anderson shares her process and techniques for surrealist collage.</p
 ><p>June 15 deadline -Step One: Gather your collage materials: fabric\, pap
 ers\, photographs\, ephemera\, buttons\, coins\, etc. Bring your materials
 to the Firehouse South Gallery by June 15.</p><p>June 22 deadline - Step Tw
 o: Anderson will recombine submitted materials and prepare them for pickup!
  Pick up your "new" supplies at the gallery before the 24th.</p><p>June 24t
 h: join us for an online workshop!</p><p>You Will Need:</p><p>Glue — Mod Po
 dge or Golden Acrylic Soft Gel Medium\, epoxy recommended for 3D items like
  buttons or coins.</p><p>Backer — matte board\, canvas\, wood panel</p><p>C
 ollage Elements - Magazines\, paper\, photos\, photocopies\, ink jet or las
 er jet print outs\, fabric\, small 3D objects like buttons\, coins</p><p>Ot
 her materials - acrylic paint\, ink\, markers\, pastels\, graphite\, charco
 al\, watercolor\, gouache</p><p>Cutting tools - scissors\, x-acto knife</p>
 <p></p><p>Janelle W Anderson creates paintings and drawings that relate to
 dreams\, memory\, consciousness\, perception of time\, existentialism\, and
  the human condition. Using symbols\, metaphors\, and various design elemen
 ts to create a collage-like aesthetic with representational imagery\, Ander
 son's work conveys a contemporary\, dream-like sense of story-telling.</p><
 p>Anderson has lived in Denver for 11 years and received a BFA in Painting
 from Metro State College of Denver in 2011. She has shown her work in galle
 ries throughout the US and was a member of Pirate: Contemporary Art for 4 y
 ears.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20210610T180859Z
LOCATION:Firehouse Art Center\, Longmont\, Colorado\, United States\, 80501
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Surrealist Collage Workshop with Janelle Anderson
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
