UID:2enugi2rbc00ej8m6jmlsc4uej@google.com
CREATED:20190413T195735Z
DESCRIPTION:SPARK works within our community to connect cultural institutio
 ns like the Firehouse with people with mild memory loss\, early stage Alzhe
 imer's or other types of dementia accompanied by their caretakers.\n\n\nGui
 ded by our two art therapists\, our participants tour the current art house
  exhibition then move to the classroom  for a "hands-on" art project. Art c
 an access different parts of the brain where words may not. Our students of
 ten vocalize a memory or describe a scene from earlier in life as a random
 color or the feel of a piece of paper spurs a recollection. \n\n Their care
 givers not only receive a cultural break from their loved ones\, but\, thos
 e vocalizations  are tangible connections to "the person still inside"\, on
 e of the most difficult\, frustrating and loving challenges a caregiver fac
 es every single day.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251007T000343Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:SPARK Program
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260906T220000Z
DTEND:20260906T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:02mc4eh0s7ihfp0ih18pk1ok12@google.com
CREATED:20260124T004444Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>Topic: Rehearsals for Remembering Artist Talk<br>Time: Sep
 6\, 2026 04:00 PM Mountain Time (US and Canada)<br>Join Zoom Meeting<br><a
 href="https://us02web.zoom.us/j/83033133846?pwd=tarimxlZDXe31bXUIYVdPX4pTT8
 oRh.1&amp\;fbclid=IwcGRvZgFleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETFLd0t5S29oWXhmeWZXdGVkc3J
 0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHtgWIgqFA5ix8pQUILbUscjrzs_ZBkiGDZSEFy
 _O-FQBxwEyakBWOMjD6vZF_aem_iueaQsWaGwezwIaSMwfF1w" target="_blank">https://
 us02web.zoom.us/j/83033133846...</a><br>Meeting ID: 830 3313 3846<br>Passco
 de: 338312<br>Kelly Leslie + Craig Cully and Whitney Sage<br>JULY 17 – SEPT
 EMBER 6\, 2026<br>EXHIBIT RECEPTION- JULY 18\, 2026<br>Rehearsals for Remem
 bering<br>Rehearsals for Remembering explores memory not as a fixed record\
 , but as an active and unstable process shaped through relationships\, obje
 cts\, and reconstruction. Through large-scale collaborative paintings and i
 ntimate accumulations of domestic imagery\, the exhibition considers how me
 aning is built through repetition\, fragmentation\, and personal associatio
 n.<br>Kelly Leslie and Craig Cully’s layered paintings emerge through an on
 going process of collaboration\, where different visual approaches overlap\
 , misalign\, and respond to one another. Their large-scale works emphasize
 tension\, balance\, and exchange\, turning the act of painting into a recor
 d of shared experience and shifting perception.<br>Whitney sage’s paintings
  and sculptural fragments approach memory through accumulation and absence.
  Images of homes\, domestic objects\, and architectural details reflect on
 personal and collective loss\, exploring how places and experiences continu
 e to linger through objects\, recollection and emotional attachment.<br>Tog
 ether\, the works suggest that remembering is a continual rehearsal\, never
  fully stable or complete. Memory shifts over time\, shaped as much by inve
 ntion and perception as by lived experience itself.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260830T161923Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rehearsals for Remembering Artist Talk- on zoom!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
