CREATED:20180103T221321Z
DESCRIPTION:Live stream tour and artist visit starts at 6:00PM. Gallery doo
 rs open at 6:30. \n\nBarbara Rudlaff presents the culmination of her Summer
  Residency in her solo exhibit “Seen.” Featuring oil portraits of lesbians
 in her social circle\, each portrait is 12”x12” and depicts the subject in
 a realist style against a white background\, wearing a mask for health and
 safety in response to our current pandemic. They are spaced in the gallery
 at least six feet apart\, commenting on distance while encouraging us to dr
 aw closer. This uniformity in presentation encourages the viewer to focus o
 n those details that make each portrait unique\, from an emphasis on the ey
 es to the subjects’ choice of mask design.\n\nIn the South Gallery\, curate
 d by Barbara Rudlaff: Quilts by Nate George: Inspired by vintage fabrics an
 d renowned paintings in the canon of western art.\n\nHead upstairs to Studi
 o C for a popup exhibition\, "Forest For The Trees\," with Firehouse Artist
  Member Joyanna Rose Gittings! \n\nMasks and social distancing required. We
  will be limiting the number of patrons in the gallery at a time.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260504T213517Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:2nd Friday Opening Reception!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
