BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20220910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20220910T200000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:5venle63e5rr80qtoh88raq68r@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Denver:20220909T180000
CREATED:20220812T194542Z
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy live music and refreshments available for donation. All r
 eceptions are free and open to the public.<br>MAIN GALLERY<br>JONO WRIGHT-
 MEMENTO VIVRE<br>Jono Wright is a Colorado painter who creates art that exp
 lores ideas about spirituality and the creative process. He believes in dis
 covering the meaning in his work during the creative process rather than il
 lustrating a preconceived idea. Portraying subject matter such as plant lif
 e\, people and objects\, he intertwines Buddhist philosophy\, Western psych
 ology and ritual theory\, fusing traditional genres of landscape\, figure\,
  still life and abstraction into unique contemporary forms.<br>“In the even
 t of a fire or natural disaster\, what would you bring with you if you had
 to flee your house?” In the wake of the Marshall Fire and the global refuge
 e crisis we are becoming aware of what’s most important to us\, the activit
 ies and objects that sustain our souls and remind us to live.<br>SOUTH GALL
 ERY<br>"RISKY BUSINESS"<br>CURATED BY JONO WRIGHT FEATURING WORKS BY...<br>
 As a play on words\, “Risky Business” refers to works that push an artists'
  comfort level. Whether moving into a medium that is not their expertise\,
 or creating something that is not typically saleable. Risky Business\, in t
 his context\, unfolds this concept and reflects back on the meaning of art\
 , creation\, and an artists’ personal experience coming through the work.<b
 r>The works on view speak to the very human fear of failure and our ability
  to transcend that fear through art-making. These four artists strive to em
 brace risk and inspire that in others through the range of works presented
 throughout this exhibition.<br>STUDIO 64- FIREHOUSE CERAMICS MEMBERS<br><a
 href="https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Ffirehouseart.org%2Fexhib
 itions%2Fupcoming-exhibitions%3Ffbclid%3DIwAR1qt0c0IeNEIdUEt_NjtX6yxR2D5UW_
 DQOj3_Ncjkq4-_zj7ZYAoctJEoY&amp\;h=AT1-4Gtoz_ADK2jyEjNWQyNigk7CX2-IwOrR7-Pi
 AfYHWJBGp847P5nxMSA6807kC-YSdVPz5JGr1mog8DezVyPg_jB00UNcQkgNUKach4bzy4q9AdI
 ncd0HXxj2GOBw5Q&amp\;__tn__=q&amp\;c[0]=AT2U2D0xK8jj1MHxGcKXc8n3lzN0A4NyHMy
 MbRte1PxzAxkzZnGg8x03JXp5H_FCNK50-omllz-yBM4CuoPtMP27dNRxcWH6HDMQoKVOGcE09-
 AJ6F2V31cCqzdXGdqbQJCuxIGbDxZsZmy5ioMhbXgs3xj1rdO9nRkU3C2LduM1bL_Z">https:/
 /firehouseart.org/exhibitions/upcoming-exhibitions</a>&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260504T213517Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:2nd Friday Exhibit Opening- Memento Vivre- Jono Wright
