UID:vuv47b2gab6m2mfh3pv5gbsgvg@google.com
CREATED:20261005T053202Z
DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/s
 chedules/activity-set/2022733\n\n\nDid you ever want to learn how to proces
 s black & white film at home? Here is your chance to shoot a roll\, roll it
  on a reel & process and dry/sleeve your negatives all at the Firehouse Art
  Center.\n\nThis is a basic\, hands-on class sharing how you can make a min
 i lab in a dark room at home. We will do all the hands on demos and labs in
  the Art Room at the Firehouse Art Center.\n\nThe instructor will provide m
 edium format 120 Holga film cameras\, a roll of B/W film to shoot & go thru
  the process of what supplies and steps to take to process your own B&W fil
 m & make a contact print.\n\nYou will walk away with a basic understanding
 of traditional B&W film processing.\n\nUpstairs classroom\nOctober 6- 6:30p
 m-8:30pm\nOctober 13- 6:30pm-8:30pm\nOctober 20- 6:30pm-8:30pm\nOctober 27-
  6:30-8:30pm\n$260 per participant.\nThis class is good for participants ag
 es 16 years old thru Adult\nInstructor: Maria Ellen Huebner\, www.mariaelle
 nhuebner.com\n\nWK 1: Class introductions\, Look at books\, check out camer
 as\, load film\, look at gear\, if time shoot a collaboration roll\, remove
  film from camera.\nAssignment\, on your own: Shoot a roll or 120 mm film b
 y the next class meeting.\n\nWK 2: Look at books\, return cameras. Introduc
 e\nnew gears. Film process Demo. Practice rolling film on reels\, roll film
  on reels.\n\nWK 3: Look at Books. Process films\, hang to dry.\n\nWK 4: Cu
 t & sleeve your negatives\, if we are lucky we can make 1 contact print fro
 m our roll. Download scanning AP Kodak Mobile Film Scanner.\n\n\nCamera & D
 evelopment Gear and Supplies Provided By Instructor\nMinimum of 4\, to maxi
 mum of 6 or 7  participants\n\nMeet your instructor:\nMaria Ellen Huebner w
 as raised on a Midwest potato farm by her Mexican migrant mother and her fi
 rst generation German-American father\, Maria discovered a passion for art
 and photography early in her life. After earning a MFA from the University
 of Wisconsin-Madison\, she has spent twenty-five years working on fine art\
 , commercial\, and journalistic projects\, while building a decade-plus tea
 ching career at institutions like the Milwaukee Area Technical College and
 Utah State University. She continues to be driven by an enduring curiosity
 about humanity and life's random circumstances. Maria frequently travels be
 tween the West and Midwest to capture compelling stories. Currently based i
 n the Boulder County\, Colorado area\, she is available for photography com
 missions\, instruction\, and mentorship\, specializing in monochromatic ima
 gery while staying versatile using digital capture as well as early alterna
 tive film photography processes. www.mariaellenhuebner.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20261005T053203Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Photography- Basic B/W Film Processing
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
