BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20261101T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20261101T110000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:ahi7s3a9fd1u190u01frgaoe32@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Denver:20261101T090000
CREATED:20261030T011059Z
DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- <u><a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-ar
 t-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1969423?source=all-activities" target="_b
 lank">https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-se
 t/1969423?source=all-activities</a></u><br><h4>9:00am - 11:00am MDT</h4><h4
 >Instructor- Kathleen M.</h4><h2><b>Class Experience</b></h2><p></p><p>Croc
 het in the Round - take your beginner crochet skills to the next level by l
 earning how to crochet in the round. This unlocks all sorts of projects inc
 luding flat round shapes like coasters and scrubbies\, to 3D shapes like am
 igurumi and plushies. Participants should already have beginner knowledge o
 n how to crochet in a row and use basic stitches.</p><p><br></p><p>Target s
 kills for this class include: magic ring\, increases in the round\, decreas
 es\, and how to close a 3D work. You are welcome to bring your own material
 s if you have them (hook\, yarn\, stitch markers\, scissors\, tapestry/darn
 ing needle). Hooks\, yarn\, and stitch markers will be available for purcha
 se in class ($5 materials fee to be collected at the beginning of class- ca
 sh or check).</p><p><br></p><p>Meet our instructor:</p><p><br></p><p>Kathle
 en is a hospice music therapist who loves to crochet. She learned how to cr
 ochet during the pandemic to help develop healthy coping skills and a new h
 obby. Kathleen enjoys creating meaningful crochet pieces including custom d
 og and cat ornaments and plushies. Kathleen has experience teaching music t
 o all ages (K-12\, college level\, and an 84 year old who wanted to learn b
 assoon)\, and is branching out now to teaching crochet in her local communi
 ty. When she’s not crocheting\, she enjoys spending time with her husband a
 nd dog\, traveling\, gardening\, and listening to music.</p><p><br></p><p>C
 lass Fee: $25</p><p>Minimum 1\, Maximum 4</p><p><br></p><p>These sessions a
 re open and work on intermediate level skills. Students should have experie
 nce with basic stitches\, which are taught during the beginners class by Am
 ber Ivey.</p><p><br></p><p>Skill level: intermediate</p><p><br></p><p>Age R
 ange: HS and older. HS students require parent to be in attendance.</p><p><
 /p><br><br><h3>Class Requirements</h3><br><ul><li>Participants under 18yrs
 of age must be accompanied by a paid and participating adult.</li></ul>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261030T011412Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intermediate Crochet
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
