DESCRIPTION:Artist Talk: Kenzie Sitterud- "HAPPY|sad"<br>RSVP HERE- <a href
 ="https://www.facebook.com/events/1012974923982422">https://www.facebook.co
 m/events/1012974923982422</a><br><br>Join us for a special artist talk with
  Kenzie Sitterud as they takes us on an emotional journey through their wor
 k\, "HAPPY|sad".<br><br>Get ready to gain a deeper understanding of their c
 reative process and to be immersed in their residency installation featurin
 g an experimental kinetic installation\, a collection of video performances
 \, concrete balloon sculptures\, AND hard-edge geometric abstract paintings
 . Happy Sad examines American privilege during times of war and the rise of
  fascism by leaning into absurdity through the use of the Mylar Happy Face
 balloon iconography and the repeated act of indulgence.<br><br>Kenzie’s wor
 k has been featured at the Denver Art Museum\, Boulder Museum of Contempora
 ry Art\, Meow Wolf Denver\, Breck Create\, Platteforum\, and various galler
 ies around the art districts of Denver.<br><br>Sitterud was an Artist-in-Re
 sidence at RedLine Contemporary Art Center from 2017-2019. While at Redline
 \, they were a Colorado Creative Industries and NEAA recipient for the 2017
  Career Advancement Grant. Sitterud received a 2019 P.S. You are Here Grant
  through Denver Arts &amp\; Venues to complete a commissioned public projec
 t for Design Workshop Foundation.<br><br>Sitterud was selected as the 2024
 Summer Artist in Residence for the Firehouse Artist Occupied Series. This p
 rogram invites emerging and established artists working in all media to exp
 lore their practice while engaging with the community.<br><span><br></span>
 <br><span>Previous resident artists include Heather Kegel\, Sean Faling\, J
 essica Forrestal\, Chris Blume\, Kaitlyn Tucek\, Roberta Restaino\, Chelsea
  Gilmore\, Barbara Rudlaff\, Amy Hoagland\, Janelle Anderson\, Jono Wright\
 , Nancy Eastman\, Makenzie Davis\, Amy Lummus and Erica Podwoiski.</span><b
 r><br>The talk will go from 3pm-4pm with an artist walkthrough from 4pm-5pm
 <br><br><br>Learn more about Kenzie here: <a href="https://l.facebook.com/l
 .php?u=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.kenziemckenzie.com%2F%3Ffbclid%3DIwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAA
 AR0Lq_WeQDrOYeffo99rL98v993UO5T8zGYj8kapR37AJsl_Z2ZXP5f_GFg_aem_vPlM_B4ZpMM
 JBWVWR2MBmg&h=AT0gE-kakzDqkSPAU9a_L9m60hV4-zfA_KXHgHfuxvx45PYwWq3f0Zdd0wWVh
 nMXio9JwNKEE-CB6hR4zFLEfArJUrd94jqM8a2PEr0AvAnExYbRilM09H8dauMYKtJKMw&__tn_
 _=q&c[0]=AT3K8YSM8jS7x7eWcSmqVESvUNkRwfe5LWVUPC1DUDsmnC4_xNXXm1BctOwVKvHCyY
 wQnMqWHM-gY_Oqbn4X-CCfiyo-8bKqXUaPIEedA_LM7ta38DVtbjsS-urA2zKpB5MtmY_FJCJvH
 4nbxmOWc8ZRtHsO1t8NUggK2Q" target="_blank"><u>www.kenziemckenzie.com</u></a
 > and on socials at @kenziesitterud.
