UID:2ioejoj7e08ksu15te6r3fp2mh@google.com
CREATED:20250531T011812Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedu
 les/activity-set/1442797?day=2025-06-07&amp\;view=cal&amp\;source=all-activ
 ities">Firehouse Art Center - Scratch your Printmaking Itch: Drypoint Intag
 lio on Plexi</a><br><br><p>In this 3 hour session\, you will learn every st
 ep of making drypoint intaglio prints\, from scratching your image into a p
 lexiglass plate\, inking it up\, and printing using a small press provided
 by the instructor. Participants will leave with 4-6 finished prints. Any ex
 perience level welcomed! Supplies and paper provided. We will work with aro
 und 5x7 inches\, so come in with a small sketch/idea for an image (simple l
 inework is best).</p><p><br></p><p>Class fee: $40</p><p>Open Seats: 10</p><
 p>Age range: 18+</p><p>Skill level: any<br><br>Meet your Instructor: Andi N
 ewberry<br><br>Andi Newberry is a printmaker and multimedia artist—sewing\,
  painting\, drawing\, and more—whose work explores the permeance of her mem
 ories\, connections with others\, and the lines drawn between memory\, stor
 ytelling\, and imagination. She earned her MFA from the University of Color
 ado\, Boulder and her BFA from Midwestern State University in Wichita Falls
 \, Texas. </p><p><br></p><p>Her printmaking and multimedia textile works ha
 ve been accepted to exhibitions for PrintAustin\, PrintHouston\, and Denver
 ’s Month of Printmaking at the Arvada Center and ArtGym in Denver. </p><p><
 br></p><p>She was selected as Boulder Library’s STUDIO24 Artist in Residenc
 e for printmaking (Jan-March 2025). She has previously taught at the Univer
 sity of Colorado\, Boulder\, Rocky Mountain College of Art and Design\, and
  Regis University.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250619T065739Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Scratch your screenprint itch!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20260602T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20260602T211500
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:989euhvg8gov0285k3flu2dbk4_R20251203T023000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Denver:20260602T193000
CREATED:20220421T183944Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://firehouseart.org/special-events/monthly-events
 /" target="_blank">Monthly Events - Firehouse Art Center</a><br><br><table>
 <tbody><tr><td><h3><b>First Tuesday Film Femmes</b></h3><h3><b><em>at Fireh
 ouse Art Center</em></b></h3><p><br></p><h3><b>This event is for women who
 make movies: You’re invited to First Tuesday Film Femmes\, aka Ladies’ Nigh
 t! We’ll gather at Firehouse\, and then go from there. We might screen some
  cool films on 16mm at the Firehouse\, or we might stroll to a nearby disti
 llery or restaurant to hang out. Please note that anyone who identifies as
 a woman is welcome at this event. Cis-women\, trans-women\, all women.</b><
 /h3><br><b><br></b><br><p dir="ltr"><b>Film Femme Fatales: Special Guest Fi
 lmmaker Sierra Cosmodis-Grove</b></p><p dir="ltr">Women and nonbinary filmm
 akers are invited to the first-ever gathering of Film Femme Fatales. This m
 onth\, we’re excited to screen a selection of short films by local filmmake
 r\, Sierra Cosmodis-Grove\, and Sierra will join us in-person for this scre
 ening and a Q&amp\;A. Sierra (she/they) graduated from the University of Co
 lorado\, Boulder in 2025 with an MFA in film. Their work is committed to al
 ternative processes\, often utilizing 16mm\, found film and hand-drawn anim
 ation. Their films feel intimate and immersive\, pulling content from their
  surroundings- images of friends\, audio of family\, to catalogue their bod
 y in space. They have shown work in festivals and galleries throughout the
 United States\, including Ann Arbor Film Festival\, Film Diary NYC\, Denver
  Digergati Experimental Festival\, Space_Space Gallery\, Sleazy Femme Film
 Festival\, Museum of Art Fort Collins\, Wicked Queer Boston and South Sound
  Experimental Film Festival. </p></td><td><br></td></tr></tbody></table><p>
 Firehouse Filmmakers is organized by Firehouse member and local filmmaker\,
  <a href="https://sunnypictures.co/" target="_blank"><u>Allison Radomski</u
 ></a>. You’re invited to follow her on Instagram (<a href="https://www.inst
 agram.com/sunnypictures.co/" target="_blank"><u>@sunnypictures.co</u></a>)
 for updates on this group. You are also welcome to subscribe to the Firehou
 se Filmmakers newsletter so that you can stay up to date on all of our even
 ts. Please click<a href="https://sunnypictures.co/firehousefilmmakers" targ
 et="_blank"> <u>here</u></a> to subscribe!</p><p>Got questions about Fireho
 use Filmmakers? Feel free to send an email to Allison at <a href="mailto:he
 llo@sunnypictures.co" target="_blank"><u>hello@sunnypictures.co</u></a>. Se
 e you soon!</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260514T211843Z
LOCATION:Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Ave\, Longmont\, CO 80501\, USA
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:First Tuesday Film Femmes- at the Firehouse
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
