DTSTART:20250923T180000Z
DTEND:20250923T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:1vum1e3vm60emdaf6u2pm58eg6@google.com
CREATED:20250725T171434Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>Come paint a Catrina painting for our Dia de los Muertos
 exhibit opening at the Firehouse Art Center!</b></p><p>Our Catrina painting
 s refer back to the Calavera Catrina – a 1910–1913 zinc etching by the Mexi
 can printmaker\, cartoon illustrator and lithographer José Guadalupe Posada
 . She is offered as a satirical portrait of those Mexican natives who\, Pos
 ada felt\, were aspiring to adopt European aristocratic traditions in the p
 re-revolution era. La Catrina has become an icon of the Mexican Día de los
 Muertos\, or Day of the Dead.</p><p>All ages are invited to join us in cele
 brating Dia de Los Muertos with community painting of Catrinas for our Dia
 de los Muertos Exhibit! Painting will occur in our Main and South galleries
  (with extra space upstairs as needed) .We hope that you will join us to cr
 eate these works of art that support and sustain the Firehouse Art Center\,
  while educating the community on this wonderful cultural event!</p><p>All
 materials for this activity are provided\, (the paper is 3’x 6’- yes they a
 re large!) but a $5-10 donation would be much appreciated!</p><p>Many times
  and days offered to fit into your schedule! Please reserve your spot!</p><
 p>If you are familiar with painting large scale and are interested in paint
 ing a canvas instead of paper\, please request a canvas by emailing <a href
 ="mailto:elaine@firehouseart.org" target="_blank">elaine@firehouseart.org</
 a>.</p><p>The painted Catrinas will be auctioned at the end of the exhibit
 to support our bilingual programing at Casa de la Esperanza and in Title 1
 SVVSD school. These programs are offered at no cost to participants.</p><p>
 Links- </p><p><a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/sche
 dules/activity-set/1539298?day=2025-09-22&amp\;view=cal&amp\;source=all-act
 ivities" target="_blank">Firehouse Art Center - Catrina Painting Days- afte
 rnoons</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250725T171434Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Catrina Painting- Please sign up using the link at the Bottom
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260411T010000Z
DTEND:20260411T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:67eoqvk3ne9v2temokjni7e96a@google.com
CREATED:20260206T233257Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Craftivism 101 with Shannon Downey</p><p>Sign up here- <a hr
 ef="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/
 1803215">Firehouse Art Center - Craftivism 101 with Badass Cross Stitch</a>
 </p><p>Get acquainted with craftivism\, learn to embroider\, stitch somethi
 ng brilliant\, and make friends—all in just 2 hours! </p><p>Craft-based act
 ivism has been used as a tool of resistance\, coalition building\, and even
  espionage! Learn from Shannon Downey—a leader in the modern craftivism mov
 ement. She will provide an introduction to the history of craftivism and wa
 ys you can get involved in the modern movement. Shannon will then teach you
  how to embroider and have you stabbing it out in no time. She guarantees y
 ou walk away feeling better than when you arrived. </p><p><br></p><p>Materi
 als provided: embroidery hoop\, embroidery floss\, 24-gauge tapestry needle
 \, quilters cotton square\, scissors\, water soluble marking pen</p><p><br>
 </p><p>Meet your instructor:</p><p>Shannon Downey aka Badass Cross Stitch i
 s a queer artist\, activist\, craftivist\, community builder\, and general
 instigator. She moves people from passive consumers of art into engaged cre
 ators. Her first book\, Let’s Move the Needle\, an activist handbook for ar
 tists\, crafters\, creatives\, and makers can be found anywhere books are s
 old. <br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260206T233257Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Craftivism 101
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20240806T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20240806T200000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:989euhvg8gov0285k3flu2dbk4@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Denver:20240806T193000
CREATED:20220421T183944Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://firehouseart.org/special-events/monthly-events
 /" target="_blank">Monthly Events - Firehouse Art Center</a><br><br><p>Fire
 house Filmmakers offers monthly meetups\, workshops\, and screening events
 for local filmmakers. We welcome filmmakers of all skill levels and artisti
 c inclinations\, from experimental animators to commercial producers\, cine
 matographers to screenwriters\, seasoned professionals to casual dabblers.
 Even if you haven’t made a movie yet\, this group is here to help you get i
 nspired.</p><p>Our primary meet-up is First Tuesday Brews\, which happens o
 n the first Tuesday of the month at 300 Suns Brewing from 6pm-8pm (moving t
 o 7:30-8:30 PM in Sept.). This is a great opportunity to get to know other
 local filmmakers and film lovers. Come by\, enjoy something delicious\, and
  make some new friends. If you’re new to the group\, just look for Allison\
 , the organizer of Firehouse Filmmakers. She’s the woman in the bright pink
  Doc Martens. Come by and join us next month!</p><p>In addition to these me
 etups\, Firehouse Filmmakers organizes a variety of events and workshops. P
 ast events include: direct animation workshops\, a very special Camera Nigh
 t featuring 16mm cameras provided by local cinematographer Garrit Speiss\,
 and screenings of member-selected short films. We’ve also partnered with ot
 her awesome local organizations like WIFMCO and Longmont Public Media to ho
 st livestreams and gear-related events.</p><p>To learn more about Firehouse
  Filmmakers or to join the mailing list for the Firehouse Filmmakers newsle
 tter (which is full of updates about upcoming workshops and events)\, pleas
 e email Allison at <a href="mailto:hello@sunnypictures.co" target="_blank">
 hello@sunnypictures.co</a>. You can also follow <a href="https://www.instag
 ram.com/firehouseartcenter/?hl=en" target="_blank">Firehouse Art Center</a>
  and <a href="https://www.instagram.com/sunnypictures.co/" target="_blank">
 Sunny Pictures</a> on Instagram for regular updates.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260514T202815Z
LOCATION:300 Suns Brewing\, 335 1st Ave Unit C\, Longmont\, CO 80501\, USA
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Filmmakers meetup- 300 Suns
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
