CREATED:20260615T162936Z
DESCRIPTION:Buy tickets here- https://thedairy.org/slaytherunway2026/\n\nTh
 e Firehouse Art Center presents Slay the Runway Designing Safe Spaces for L
 GBTQIA+ Youth\nJune 27 @ 6:30 pm\n$11.50 – $17.25\n\nSlay the Runway is a F
 irehouse Art Center Fashion Design program offered at no cost to LGBTQIA+ y
 outh and Youth allies to support self-expression. Our goal is to be a safe
 space for teens to explore their own true style in a Gender Expansive and s
 upportive community.\n\nWith cohorts in Longmont and Boulder\, instructors
 start with simple projects that improve student sewing and design skills. A
 s confidence builds\, students are challenged to develop their own self-ide
 ntity as they create an outfit for the showcase. At the fashion show\, stud
 ents unveil something they’ve created in their style and voice while surrou
 nded by a community sharing their life experiences. In addition to garment
 construction and design\, participants will work with make-up artists and c
 horeographers to refine their debuts. While there are fashion camps and sew
 ing classes in the area\, no other local offerings address the issue of saf
 e spaces for gender-expansive youth with this depth of creativity\, and it
 is the only program that is no cost to participants.\n\nSlay the Runway’s g
 oal is to create an affirming and accessible space where creativity\, expre
 ssion\, and positive self-image are celebrated.\n\nThis program is made pos
 sible by SCFD\, the City of Longmont\, OASOS\, CU Boulder\, your donations\
 , and the never ending enthusiasm and passion of the Slay Team!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260615T162936Z
LOCATION:Dairy Arts Center\, 2590 Walnut St\, Boulder\, CO 80302\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Slay the Runway at the Dairy Center
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
