CREATED:20251103T213923Z
DESCRIPTION:More info and rsvp here- <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=
 https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1618
 584&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1762637940618995&amp\;usg=AOvVa
 w34HgEYkWXfmmfPQWXiR47v" target="_blank">https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse
 -art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1618584</a><br><br><br>Class Experienc
 e<br>This class is perfect for total beginners wanting to get started on th
 eir crochet journey. You&#39\;ll learn how to hold the hook and yarn\, and
 complete basic crochet stitches.<br><br>Class fee: $20 per person (each att
 endee will be given yarn\, hook\, and handout to take home).<br><br>Ages 16
 +<br><br>Maximum class size of 10 people.<br><br>Offering the same class ev
 ery month on the second Monday of the month <br><br>Meet your instructor: A
 mber Ivey<br><br>Although Amber Ivey is technically an artistic dabbler\, e
 njoying a variety of arts and crafts\, she has been crocheting for over 10
 years\, and has a plethora of crochet teaching experience thanks to running
  the Longmont Community Crochet Guild since 2018. Prior to running the guil
 d\, she was a full time mom\, and prior to becoming a mom she worked as a m
 iddle school math teacher. Her past interests have seen her try pottery\, a
 cting\, furniture refinishing\, poetry writing\, black and white photograph
 y\, bookbinding\, ballroom dancing\, upholstery\, jewelry making\, sewing\,
  embroidery\, collage\, graphic design\, and knitting. She has lived in Mia
 mi\, NYC\, and France\, and dreams of one day being fluent in Spanish and v
 isiting Cuba.<br><br>What To Bring<br>each attendee will be given yarn\, ho
 ok\, and handout to take home<br>You don&#39\;t NEED to bring any supplies\
 , but if you have yarn and/or hooks already\, you can bring them and we can
  discuss whether or not they are good for beginners.<br>It would also be gr
 eat to know ahead of time if folks are *right* handed or *left* handed!!
LAST-MODIFIED:20251110T050613Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learn to crochet
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
