DTSTART:20261205T170000Z
DTEND:20261205T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:7qhcsqgojp91vdv1s4jc2lg2m0@google.com
CREATED:20260817T174930Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Sign up here- <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://
 www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1993333&amp\
 ;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1787420964218890&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1XzFOqY
 iLrb3wbv-8G7VLk" target="_blank">Firehouse Art Center - Color Curious</a> <
 /p><p>  Are you color curious? Join us for an exploration of the use of col
 or in any application. This workshop isn’t just for artists: it&#39\;s for
 anyone who wants to become more confident with color. We play with color co
 mbinations and palettes and chat about how to make color pop\, glow or soot
 h. Everyone will have the opportunity to talk about color challenges in the
 ir own projects. This is a great group activity… bring friends and snacks a
 nd be ready to have fun!</p><p>Class Fee/Materials Fee: $35</p><p>Age Range
 : Adults 15+</p><p>Class duration- 2 hours</p><p>Location- south gallery</p
 ><p><br></p><p>Karrie Steely is an artist\, instructor\, and arts community
  builder. She is passionate about sharing the gifts of a lifelong commitmen
 t to creativity and curiosity. Collaborators\, cohorts and students alike a
 re inspired by her joy and enthusiasm.</p><p> </p><p>Karrie’s award-winning
  artwork has been exhibited in Colorado\, Nebraska and Kansas. So far\, 202
 6 projects have included an artist residency at the Robert Henri Museum and
  Gallery where she taught workshops\, leading community murals in Nebraska\
 , and judging at the Nebraska State Fair. She was a 2023-2025 Rural Regener
 ator Fellow with Springboard for the Arts. She recently moved back to her n
 ative Colorado\, where she continues to lead workshops and paint murals.</p
 >
LAST-MODIFIED:20260817T174930Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Color Curious
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
