CREATED:20250429T234932Z
DESCRIPTION:\nArtists As Activists Presentation\n“Exploring and Understandi
 ng Activist Art”\n\nFrom performance art by Yoko Ono to street art by Banks
 y\, from Keith Haring’s paintings by Picasso’s Guernica\, artists have used
  their work to shed light on social issues and as calls-to-action.\n\nPrese
 ntation includes:\n A collection of historic and current activist art\n F
 orms and treatments found in activist art: literal\, humorous / ironic\, in
 teractive\, multi-faceted\, in-a-series\, ironic\n The creation of activis
 t art using visual inspiration\, metaphor\, appropriation\n The process of
  creating activist art: connecting / reacting\, analyzing / reading\n In a
 ddition\, a brief introduction to Artists As Activists – the mission\, feat
 ures\, mechanics and benefits of the organization will be covered.\n\nAbout
  the speaker: As a promoter and advocate of activist art to raise awareness
  and stimulate dialogue as a vehicle for change\, Lynden Cline is the found
 er and curator of Artists As Activists.
LAST-MODIFIED:20250502T212311Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:“Exploring and Understanding Activist Art”- Artists as Activists
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
