CREATED:20260514T202934Z
DESCRIPTION:Monthly Events - Firehouse Art Center\n\nReserve your spot here
 -  https://www.eventbrite.com/e/introduction-to-16mm-filmmaking-with-the-bo
 lex-tickets-1992439763969 \n\nIntro to 16mm Filmmaking at Firehouse Art Cen
 ter\n\nWant to shoot a movie on film? At this workshop\, we’ll talk about h
 ow to get started with a Bolex 16mm camera\, which is a relatively simple (
 and fun!) way to work with celluloid.  Although lots of people think of the
  Bolex as a camera for beginners or students\, there are so many amazing an
 d accomplished filmmakers — like Jodie Mack— who choose to work with this c
 amera because of it’s unique advantages. Come see what the hype is about at
  this 16mm film workshop.\nThe Bolex camera is a great way to get started w
 ith 16mm filmmaking. If you’ve ever wanted to learn how to work with real f
 ilm\, this introductory workshop is for you. Although some see the Bolex as
  a camera used exclusively by students or beginners\, there are many establ
 ished filmmakers who choose to use this camera because of its unique advant
 ages. Join us as we learn more about how it works. Participation will be ca
 pped at 15 people. This event will be free\, but you’ll have to register. R
 egistration will \n\nFirehouse Filmmakers is organized by Firehouse member
 and local filmmaker\, Allison Radomski. You’re invited to follow her on Ins
 tagram (@sunnypictures.co) for updates on this group. You are also welcome
 to subscribe to the Firehouse Filmmakers newsletter so that you can stay up
  to date on all of our events. Please click here to subscribe!\nGot questio
 ns about Firehouse Filmmakers? Feel free to send an email to Allison at hel
 lo@sunnypictures.co. See you soon!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260624T182917Z
LOCATION:Firehouse Art Center\, 667 4th Ave\, Longmont\, CO 80501\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intro to 16mm Filmmaking
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
