DTSTART:20250822T003000Z
DTEND:20250822T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:13ppk50il5d5r2f4qbt3e5hmda@google.com
CREATED:20250728T165531Z
DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- <a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-c
 enter-1/schedules/activity-set/1567306">Firehouse Art Center - "How to Play
  in the Dark with Art"</a><br><br><p>"How to Play in the Dark with Art" Com
 e explore the power of art making to move through the challenges\, blocks\,
  and wounds that we can't really run away from (even if we try to). When we
  have the tools to move through our struggles\, it opens you up to a whole
 new path forward.  You will be invited into a therapeutic art experience ut
 ilizing presence\, curiosity\, compassion\, play\, imagination\, and creati
 ve expression. </p><p><br></p><p>Come on\, you know you are curious…I love
 to say that art is an experiment and you never know what you will learn alo
 ng the way. Maybe you will discover something about yourself that you have
 been looking for. And creating in community makes it even more powerful and
  rich. If your inner-critic is holding you back\, know that NO ART EXPERIEN
 CE IS NEEDED!!! AND ALL ART MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED!!! Just bring your curio
 us mind and playful spirit. Resistance and fear is also welcome.</p><p>____
 ____________________<br>About the Facilitator:<br>Danielle Rifkin\, LPC\, A
 TR is the owner of How To Play In The Dark. She is a Somatic\, Art &amp\; P
 lay Therapist\, and Grief Ritualist. She has been running grief circles\, a
 rt groups\, and other experiential offerings for over a decade. She got her
  Master's degree from Naropa University in Transpersonal Psychology and has
  worked in a variety of therapeutic settings in her career. She has facilit
 ated hundreds of groups where she emphasizes creating spaces that allow for
  authenticity and feeling safe enough to show all parts of themselves.<br><
 br><br>Cost- $40 (Sliding scale is available by reaching out to <a href="ma
 ilto:daniellerifkin@riseuprooted.org" target="_blank">daniellerifkin@riseup
 rooted.org</a>)</p><p>Materials provided<br>Age: 18+<br>Minimum: 3 students
  Maximum: 12 students<br>No experience needed</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250728T165536Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:How to Play in the Dark with Art Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
