DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/s
 chedules/activity-set/1340726?source=all-activities\n\nContinuing Beginner
 and Intermediate Wheel: Age 16+. \n\nFor those with experience with ceramic
 s who wish to receive personalized training on topics including centering\,
  wedging\, throwing techniques\, shaping\, trimming\, glazing and building
 compound forms such as teapots.\n\nStudents will increase their understandi
 ng of all basic phases of producing satisfying projects and will have the o
 pportunity to explore individual goals such as larger pieces\, taller piece
 s\, thinner pieces\, jars\, lids\, handles\, etc. This class will be highly
  beneficial for students who have time to take advantage of the included op
 en studio time. \n\nExcellent demos and resources will be provided and inde
 pendent projects will be encouraged. This class will be ideal for new stude
 nts\, continuing students and those who have taken a ceramics class in the
 past.\n\nMax\, 6 people. \n$290\n\n8 week classes\, 2.5 hours\, 1 day a wee
 k\n\nClasses meet once a week for 2.5 hours in the FAC Ceramics Studio for
 eight weeks (20 hours of total instruction)\, and are limited in size to 6
 students. Access to open studio hours is included for the duration of the c
 lass and one week following. A basic tool kit is available for purchase if
 you do not have personal tools. You can purchase here-https://firehouseart.
 org/product/tool-kit/.\n A 20 lb bag of student clay is provided to each st
 udent\, along with a half-shelf and cubby. Additional clay is available for
  purchase.\n\nStudio classes are for adults ages 18 and over (students 16+
 may attend classes when accompanied by a paying adult).\n\nCourse Policies\
 nRefunds are not allowed after the course begins. Refunds requested during
 the week prior to the start of the class will be honored at 50%. Refunds re
 quested prior to this will be honored minus fees. If you would like to requ
 est a refund\, email education@firehouseart.org.\n\nStudio etiquette\nOpen
 studio:\nStudents are encouraged to come in on their own time to work on th
 eir projects during Open Studio hours (posted online). Entry to studio outs
 ide of Open Studio hours will be disabled via entry system.\n\nCleaning:\nP
 lease be sure to clean up the area you are working in\, including:\n\nHandb
 uilding tables - wipe down after use\nGlaze area - wipe down any spills\, c
 ountertops\, and buckets\nStudio tools - clean before putting back in drawe
 r\n\nNoise:\nPlease use headphones when listening to music or podcasts\, an
 d please take phone calls outside.\nStorage:\nThere is shelving provided fo
 r each class in the classroom. This can be used for the duration of the cla
 ss\; however\, once class is over these shelves must be cleared. Anything l
 eft behind after the two week grace period concludes will be assumed abando
 ned and then discarded.\n\nClay:\nWe will provide student clay for the sess
 ion (one 20 lb bag per student) and additional clay is available for purcha
 se. You can use outside clay\, but it must be cone 5 and above.\n\nYour Ins
 tructor- Rick Thompson\nI love art\, mostly enjoying\, but also creating. T
 here is a skill in the seeing\, in the hearing\, in the feeling and if you
 love food\, the tasting. These requisite skills must be developed in tandem
  with brush strokes and shutter clicks. It is in developing these skills th
 at one amplifies an appreciation for art and for life itself. My ceramics\,
  photography and other forms of art hope to make a small contribution to a
 world full of beautiful and curious  things. I particularly enjoy delightfu
 lly crafted bowls and mugs paired with the perfect ramen or morning coffee.
  In this way\, eating and drinking become a daily act of beauty.\n\nAs a te
 chnologist\, I have been teaching adults and youth for several decades. I l
 ove helping people to exceed their goals and go beyond what they thought po
 ssible.
LAST-MODIFIED:20250311T143651Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intermediate Wheel Throwing
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
