CREATED:20250408T190526Z
DESCRIPTION:For more info\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/1242425213972557
 \n\n\nSouth Gallery: Parallel Play 2: An Ekphrastic Exhibit presented by th
 e Firehouse Writers and Artists\nThe Firehouse Art Center is home to both p
 racticing visual artists and writers. Annually for April\, which is Month o
 f Poetry\, these writers and artists collaborate to present an ekphrasis ba
 sed exhibit. Ekphrasis is a Greek word meaning “a literary device that desc
 ribes a work of art.”. Ekphrasis in ancient Greece was the skill of describ
 ing a thing with vivid detail. Today\, the term refers to writing in respon
 se to an artwork. The annual writers/artists exhibit expands on the definit
 ion of ekphrasis by having artists make artworks based on the works of auth
 ors as well as authors reacting to visual art.\n\nMuch like the game “Telep
 hone”\, subtle shifts in meaning may be accomplished by translating an auth
 or’s work into another language\, giving both works multiple layers.\nArtis
 t Reading and Presentation: Saturday\, April 19\, 12pm-1pm- followed by a c
 ommunity protest from 1-2pm\n\nParticipating Writers and Artists:\nAspen Ev
 erett\nKathryn Hall\nJacki Massaro\nBetsy Anderson\nDeborah Kelly\nTerri Kr
 ause\nJoshua C D Robinson\nElaine Waterman\nRiley Ann\nKathy Rush
LAST-MODIFIED:20250418T005849Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Poetry/Artist work presentation/potluck
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
