DESCRIPTION:<p>"Bending Wood"   </p><p>2 day workshop- you must attend Dec
 6 and 7th workshops</p><p><a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-c
 enter-1/schedules/activity-set/1695415" target="_blank">https://www.hisawye
 r.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1695415</a></p><p>This
 two day adult workshop will explore the art of bending wood using the free-
 form bent lamination technique.  Participants will create unique shapes tha
 t will be included in a community art piece exhibited at the Firehouse duri
 ng the Winter Residency culminating exhibit.  Following the exhibit\, parti
 cipants will be able to take their creations home.  </p><p><br></p><p>$50/p
 erson includes all materials and supplies\,  5-10 participants\, no prior w
 oodworking experience needed</p><p><br></p><p>Meet your instructor</p><p>Do
 ug Felkley:</p><p>I am a teacher\, a sculptor\, and a sometimes reluctant f
 urniture maker.  After retiring from a decades long career as a gymnastics
 coach\, I felt it was time to explore an entirely new second career.  This
 desire for something new led me to study fine furniture making and design a
 t Red Rocks Community College.  Upon completion of the program I began taki
 ng commissions for custom furniture pieces\, something that I found extreme
 ly stressful.  Looking for a new creative outlet\, I began experimenting wi
 th wood focused sculpture and found expression for my creative ideas.  Alth
 ough I felt deeply connected to this creative path\, I missed working with
 kids\, and out of nowhere an opportunity to be a middle school woodworking
 teacher showed up!  Now\, teaching woodworking as an art form gives me an o
 utlet for both of my passions\, teaching and art.  </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251117T154532Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bending Wood Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
