DESCRIPTION:After School Origami/Paper Folding with Junghwa<br>$35/class<br
 >Tickets here- <a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/sch
 edules/activity-set/1219049">Firehouse Art Center - After School Origami/Pa
 per Folding</a><br><p>Origami offers numerous benefits\, including enhancin
 g creativity\,  improving concentration and patience\, and strengthening ha
 nd-eye coordination. It also provides the joy of making things by hand and
 a  sense of accomplishment. In this class\, you will learn techniques rangi
 ng from basic to advanced\, with all materials included in the class  fee.<
 br><br>  Class Content:<br>- Basic and advanced origami techniques<br>- Hea
 rts and heart-shaped boxes\, rabbits and envelopes<br>- Butterflies\, boxes
 \, and four-leaf clovers<br>- Flowers\, animals\, dresses<br>- Cranes\, bro
 oches\, heart-shaped boxes\, and more<br><br>If you are interested in origa
 mi\, join us for a fun and meaningful experience<br><br>Class fee $35(each
 class)<br>Age Range: 6-13 years<br>Class Size: Minimum 1 student\, maximum
 6 students<br>Skill Level: All levels are welcome<br>Meet your Instructor:<
 br>I'm Junghwa Lee\, I am married with two children. I originally came from
  South Korea in 1998 and have been living in Longmont since 2001. I teach w
 atercolor painting classes to beginners and intermediate students.</p><p><b
 r></p><p>Pre-registration and confirmation are required.</p><p>If there are
  no registrations 24 hours before the class starts\, the class will be canc
 eled.</p><p>Students must contact the instructor directly to arrange except
 ions.</p><p>Missed classes by students will result in credit but not refund
 s.</p>
