DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><p>OPENING TODAY</p><p>South Gallery: Parallel Pl
 ay 2: An Ekphrastic Exhibit presented by the Firehouse Writers and Artists<
 /p><p></p><p><span>The Firehouse Art Center is home to both practicing visu
 al artists and writers. Annually for April\, which is Month of Poetry\, the
 se writers and artists collaborate to present an ekphrasis based exhibit. E
 kphrasis is a Greek word meaning “a literary device that describes a work o
 f art.”. Ekphrasis in ancient Greece was the skill of describing a thing wi
 th vivid detail. Today\, the term refers to writing in response to an artwo
 rk. The annual writers/artists exhibit expands on the definition of ekphras
 is by having artists make artworks based on the works of authors as well as
  authors reacting to visual art.  Presentation is scheduled for April 19 fr
 om 12pm-2pm.</span></p><p>Wednesday: 12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (open to walk in gu
 ests)</p><p>Thursday: 12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (open to walk in guests)</p><p>Fri
 day: 12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (open to walk in guests)</p><p>Saturday: 12:00 pm –
  5:00 pm (open to walk in guests)<br></p><p>Sunday:  12:00 pm – 5:00 pm (op
 en to walk in guests)<br></p><p>Please check the calendar for any closures
 due to installation\, 2nd Fridays or private events.</p><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260525T020314Z
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:GALLERY HOURS- 12PM-5PM
