DESCRIPTION:What is artist circle?  A bunch of artists of all mediums sit d
 own and create in the same space while sharing mealtime\, conversation and
 camaraderie. <br><br><br>Laugh\, get out and meet people\, work on your own
  stuff and see what everyone else is working on.  We meet on the 2nd Monday
  of the month.<br><br>This new group plans to meet on the second Monday of
 every month from 12:00 noon - 2:30 PM with the goal of working on individua
 l projects while sharing creative energies and inspiration and conversation
  in a casual\, supportive gathering. All interested individuals are invited
  to bring whatever creative project they have in process to work on. No fee
 s. Donations to The Firehouse are welcomed but not required. Bring a friend
  or meet new ones. If you have any questions and/ or think you might come\,
  please send a text to Kathy Hall at 303-746-0629 so we know approximately
 how many to set up for. Thank you.<br><br>Sign up here- <a href="https://ww
 w.eventbrite.com/e/firehouse-artists-circle-tickets-372984054347">Firehouse
  Artist's Circle Tickets\, Multiple Dates | Eventbrite</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261030T012229Z
LOCATION:Firehouse Art Center\, Longmont\, Colorado\, United States\, 80501
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Firehouse Artist's Circle- this week at Old TOwn Marketplace
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20251110T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20251110T200000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;UNTIL=20251115T065959Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:6v3n6q4ocd6js4jqhbb67rvduq@google.com
CREATED:20250815T180645Z
DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www
 .hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1442000?source%
 3Dall-activities&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1755713197629899&a
 mp\;usg=AOvVaw1ENfyvqrL1MFc6UpzU7170" target="_blank">Firehouse Art Center
 - Intro to Pastels</a><br><br><p>This four day Pastel intensive\, will buil
 d a strong foundation of knowledge that will jump-start your exploration of
  the pastel medium. Students will have the opportunity to experience a vari
 ety of pastel materials through hands-on experience.<br><br>Dates: November
  10-13</p><p>Time- 6pm-8pm</p><p>Cost: $160 <br>Materials: a $65 Materials
 fee (check to the instructor) </p><p><br></p><p>Minimum students: 4<br>Maxi
 mum students: 8<br>Age range: Over 18<br><br>Additional supply list: For th
 ose wanting to expand their pastel collection I will provide a list of sugg
 ested brands and colors once registered. Participants will receive a 10% di
 scount on pastels and paper at Dakota Art Pastels.<br><br><strong><b>Day 1<
 /b></strong></p><p>Students will have the opportunity to experience a varie
 ty of pastel materials through hands-on experience.<br>- Brief discussion o
 n Pastels<br>- What’s so great about pastels<br>- Pastel types: Hard pastel
 s\, soft pastels\, pan pastels and pencils<br>- A chart of pastels types th
 at list pastels from hard to softest will be provided<br>- The relationship
  between pastel paper and pastels<br>- There will be several short exercise
 s that allow students to work with different pastel brands and understand w
 hat makes each unique and how differently each feels when applied to the di
 fferent types of paper.<br>- The sample material kit purchased for this cla
 ss will have 6 sheets of paper\, enough for the workshop series of exercise
 s and paintings.  Six different brands of pastels will also be included.<br
 ></p><p><strong><b>Day 2<br>- </b></strong>Value studies through hands-on e
 xperience using only one dark\, one medium and one light pastel.</p><p>- A
 discussion of the importance of value<br>- A  b/w simple landscape will be
 provided to paint from<br>- A value chart will be provided<br>- After caref
 ul study of the provided images values\, students will paint\, light\, medi
 um and dark shapes of the image<br></p><p><strong><b>Day 3</b></strong></p>
 <p>- Discussion on tools and blending techniques.<br>- Discussion on under
 painting<br>- Complementary or analogous<br>- Use of rubbing alcohol<br>- B
 lending techniques and supplies<br>- Examine different blender types and fi
 nger covers<br>- Fixatives<br>- Ooops - how do I get rid of this mistake -
 spray air\, bristal brushes\, etc.<br></p><p>Day 4<br>Students will be enco
 uraged to bring in a printout of something they would like to paint before
 this class or choose from images I provide. 8.5 x 11 prints from a computer
  printer should be used.        <br>All of the above classes will be incorp
 orated to produce a pastel of their chosen image.<br><br>Day 5<br>Optional
 - for those students who want more class time/instruction to finish. Class
 critique.</p><p><br></p><p>Instructor Bio</p><p>Patricia Fabian was born in
  Chicago\, Illinois in 1957. She received a BFA in Graphic Design from the
 University of Illinois in 1981. In her over 40 year career as a graphic des
 igner she understood and practiced the importance of color theory\, hierarc
 hy and composition. These three concepts greatly influence her current artw
 ork. Her work is also influenced by the precision and accuracy required of
 her early medical art education. Here her love of life drawing was fostered
 . She fell in love with pastel with her first purchase in 2013. “The medium
  to me is the most like life drawing.” She also works in paper maché\, eco-
 dyed paper\, collage\, water color\, acrylics and oil.</p><p><br></p><p>Com
 position is of upmost importance to her. When out exploring she thrills at
 the beauty of the natural world and the leading compositions presented. Pat
 ricia will paint plein air\, but prefers taking a snap shot and working in
 her studio where she finds the luxury of time\, materials and enhancing the
  work’s composition perfect for her artistic style.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250815T180645Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intro to Pastels with Patty Fabian
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
