BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20261101T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20261101T110000
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;UNTIL=20261206T065959Z;BYDAY=1SU
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:ahi7s3a9fd1u190u01frgaoe32@google.com
CREATED:20261030T011059Z
DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- <u><a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-ar
 t-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1969423?source=all-activities" target="_b
 lank">https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-se
 t/1969423?source=all-activities</a></u><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><h4>9:00
 am - 11:00am MDT</h4><br><br><br><br><br>Location<br><h4>667 4th Ave\, Long
 mont\, CO 80501</h4><br><br><br><br>Instructor<br><h4>Kathleen M.</h4><br><
 br><br><br>Capacity<br><h4>7 students</h4><br><hr /><h2><b>Class Experience
 </b></h2><br><p></p><p>Crochet in the Round - take your beginner crochet sk
 ills to the next level by learning how to crochet in the round. This unlock
 s all sorts of projects including flat round shapes like coasters and scrub
 bies\, to 3D shapes like amigurumi and plushies. Participants should alread
 y have beginner knowledge on how to crochet in a row and use basic stitches
 .</p><p><br></p><p>Target skills for this class include: magic ring\, incre
 ases in the round\, decreases\, and how to close a 3D work. You are welcome
  to bring your own materials if you have them (hook\, yarn\, stitch markers
 \, scissors\, tapestry/darning needle). Hooks\, yarn\, and stitch markers w
 ill be available for purchase in class ($5 materials fee to be collected at
  the beginning of class- cash or check).</p><p><br></p><p>Meet our instruct
 or:</p><p><br></p><p>Kathleen is a hospice music therapist who loves to cro
 chet. She learned how to crochet during the pandemic to help develop health
 y coping skills and a new hobby. Kathleen enjoys creating meaningful croche
 t pieces including custom dog and cat ornaments and plushies. Kathleen has
 experience teaching music to all ages (K-12\, college level\, and an 84 yea
 r old who wanted to learn bassoon)\, and is branching out now to teaching c
 rochet in her local community. When she’s not crocheting\, she enjoys spend
 ing time with her husband and dog\, traveling\, gardening\, and listening t
 o music.</p><p><br></p><p>Class Fee: $25</p><p>Minimum 1\, Maximum 4</p><p>
 <br></p><p>These sessions are open and work on intermediate level skills. S
 tudents should have experience with basic stitches\, which are taught durin
 g the beginners class by Amber Ivey.</p><p><br></p><p>Skill level: intermed
 iate</p><p><br></p><p>Age Range: HS and older. HS students require parent t
 o be in attendance.</p><p></p><br><br><h3>Class Requirements</h3><br><ul><l
 i>Participants under 18yrs of age must be accompanied by a paid and partici
 pating adult.</li></ul>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261030T011412Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intermediate Crochet
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
