DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20260822T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20260822T120000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;UNTIL=20261004T055959Z;BYDAY=SA
EXDATE;TZID=America/Denver:20260912T090000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:6micr4r2hv20dc4ja73nvrnfhl@google.com
CREATED:20260724T192953Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><br><br><br><h1><b>Sign up here- </b><a href="https://www.g
 oogle.com/url?q=https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/a
 ctivity-set/1960332?source%3Dall-activities&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&
 amp\;ust=1785353380915443&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1mdU35xhdiD58aBlCL2LqD" target="_b
 lank">Firehouse Art Center - Beginner Wheel Throwing Saturday AM</a> </h1><
 h1> <b>Beginner Wheel Throwing Saturday AM</b></h1><br><br><h4><b>Class Exp
 erience</b></h4><br><br><p></p><p>Beginner Wheel Throwing- Saturday morning
 </p><p>This class is 7 weeks total as we are skipping September 12 for ArtW
 alk.<br>This course is designed to teach the fundamentals of working with c
 lay on the potter’s wheel—no prior experience is necessary. Students will b
 e introduced to the basics of centering\, opening\, pulling walls\, trimmin
 g and surface decoration.  <br><br>6 week classes\, 3 hours\, 1 day a week\
 , for 6 weeks\, in a group of up to 5. $280\, Age 18+<br><br>Classes meet o
 nce a week for 3 hours in the FAC Ceramics Studio for six weeks (18 hours o
 f total instruction)\, and are limited in size to 5 students. Access to ope
 n studio hours is included for the duration of the class and one week follo
 wing. While communal tools are available\, a basic tool kit will also need
 to be purchased at the start of the session. You can purchase here-<a href=
 "https://www.google.com/url?q=https://firehouseart.org/product/tool-kit/.&a
 mp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1785353380915443&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1TIN
 n6o4vAi1uiUowNeEH_" target="_blank">https://firehouseart.org/product/tool-k
 it/.</a></p><p> A 20 lb bag of reclaim clay is provided to each student\, a
 long with a shelf and cubby. Additional clay is available for purchase.<br>
 <br>Studio classes are for adults ages 18 and over (students 16+ may attend
  classes when accompanied by a paying adult).<br><br>Week 1: Introduction t
 o working at the FAC Ceramics Studio and throwing on the wheel<br>Week 2: I
 ntroduction to the terminology and protocols of throwing<br>Week 3: Introdu
 ction to basic trimming and throwing techniques<br>Week 4: Introduction to
 basic forms and shapes<br>Week 5: Introduction to glazing<br>Week 6: Introd
 uction to basic glazing techniques and final review<br>Course Policies<br>R
 efunds are not allowed after the course begins. Refunds requested during th
 e week prior to the start of the class will be honored at 50%. Refunds requ
 ested prior to this will be honored minus Sawyer  fees. If you would like t
 o request a refund\, email <a href="mailto:info@firehouseart.org" target="_
 blank">info@firehouseart.org</a>.<br><br>Studio classes are for adults ages
  18 and over (students 16+ may attend classes when accompanied by a paying
 adult).<br><br>Studio etiquette<br><br>Open studio:<br>Students are encoura
 ged to come in on their own time to work on their projects during Open Stud
 io hours (posted online and in the classroom). Entry to studio outside of O
 pen Studio hours will be disabled via entry system.<br><br>Cleaning:<br>Ple
 ase be sure to clean up the area you are working in\, including:<br><br>Han
 dbuilding tables - wipe down after use<br><br>Glaze area - wipe down any sp
 ills\, countertops\, and buckets<br><br>Studio tools - clean before putting
  back in drawer<br><br>Noise:<br>Please use headphones when listening to mu
 sic or podcasts\, and please take phone calls outside.<br>Storage:<br>There
  is shelving provided for each class in the classroom. This can be used for
  the duration of the class\; however\, once class is over these shelves mus
 t be cleared. Anything left behind after the two week grace period conclude
 s will be assumed abandoned and then discarded.<br><br>Clay:<br>We will pro
 vide clay for the session (one 20 lb bag of reclaim per student) and additi
 onal clay is available for purchase. You can use outside clay\, but it must
  be cone 5 and above.<br><br>Your Instructor- Beau Bryant<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260724T193019Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Beginners Wheelthrowing
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20251012T193000Z
DTEND:20251012T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:3vctdlcmlfpmdcoc3fia94om00@google.com
CREATED:20250818T230508Z
DESCRIPTION:<h1><b>Ojos de Dios: A Mindful Weaving Journey</b></h1><br><b>S
 ign up here- </b><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.hisawyer
 .com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1595141&amp\;sa=D&amp\;s
 ource=calendar&amp\;ust=1755989194722771&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1PAba17sD5XGDbW0srI
 OyL" target="_blank">https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedu
 les/activity-set/1595141</a><br><br><p>Join artist Michelle Sepulveda for a
  2.5-hour workshop that blends mindful portal weaving with guided reflectio
 n </p><p>What to expect: </p><p>We’ll begin with a short grounding breathwo
 rk and meditation to center the mind and body</p><p>Learn about the origins
  through the meditative process of creating an Ojo de Dios (God’s Eye) —als
 o envisioned here as a personal portal—you’ll explore themes of realignment
 \, grounding\, and self-awareness. We’ll weave with intention\, allowing co
 lor\, texture\, and form to guide your process. Students  will learn five d
 ifferent weaving patterns on a 8 point portal using dowels &amp\; yarn</p><
 p>The session will close with journaling prompts designed to deepen your in
 sights and help you integrate your experience. You’ll leave with a meaningf
 ul woven piece—either one 11-inch or two 5.5-inch Ojos—that serves as a las
 ting reminder of balance and purpose.</p><p>All materials provided. No prio
 r experience needed—just an open heart\, mind and curious hands. </p><p>Mee
 t your instructor: Michelle Sepulveda</p><p>I am a Chicanx artist driven by
  curiosity\, cultural connection\, and a deep appreciation for creative exp
 ression. Born and raised in Brighton and Ft. Lupton\, Colorado\, my artisti
 c journey began at a young age\, nurtured by my family’s encouragement to e
 xplore my talents and embrace what sparks my imagination. My grandmother\,
 in particular\, played a pivotal role in shaping my creative process—teachi
 ng me patience\, reflection\, and the beauty of experimentation through art
 \, baking\, and crafting.</p><p>Fascinated by the world around me\, I use m
 ixed media &amp\; fiber\, folk art to weave elements of my Chicana/Indigeno
 us heritage with a playful and thought-provoking approach. My work often ch
 allenges societal norms while honoring the traditions and stories of my anc
 estors. I am drawn to non-traditional materials\, allowing my inner child t
 o guide me in discovering new ways to create and express myself.</p><p><br>
 </p><p>Ages 15 &amp\; up</p><p>Class fee $33</p><p>Max: 15</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250818T230509Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ojos de Dios: A Mindful Weaving Journey
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
