BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260503T190000Z
DTEND:20260503T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:6sq9l9j28c3cp1p1sel3o6s6ts@google.com
CREATED:20260206T232633Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Sign up here- <a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-ar
 t-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1802421">Firehouse Art Center - Pride Mon
 th Art Sampler</a></p><p>We are partnering with the Longmont Library and Bu
 tterscotch Studios to present an art exhibit for Pride to show at the libra
 ry on June 7th.  The pieces in the show will be created over a series of 5
 art classes at the Firehouse.  The whole program only costs $100! You will
 have a chance to experience different mediums from acrylic\, to clay\, to f
 abric! All abilities welcome- no artistic experience necessary! (Age 14+) <
 /p><p><br></p><p>May 3 (FIRST CLASS IS ON SUNDAY)- Let your freak flag fly-
  Create your own flag or banner that represents you! You'll learn what make
 s a "good" flag (keep it simple silly!) and create one that is all about yo
 u.  You'll get to take that flag home to fly proudly.</p><p><br></p><p>Satu
 rday- May 9- 1:30- 3:30- The Art of Healing: A guided Artistic Experience</
 p><p>Experience the power of art to unlock healing and transformation.  Thi
 s introspective artistic activity will incorporate meditative practices and
  personal introspection with ceramic painting\, inviting you to foster conn
 ection within yourself and with those around you to create something beauti
 ful.  </p><p>Meet your instructor- Amber Cantorna-Wylde (she/her) is a nati
 onal speaker\, consultant\, and community healer passionate about fostering
  a world of acceptance and belonging. She’s the author of three books\, the
  founder the Unashamed Love Collective which ran for 10 seasons\, and she n
 ow owns a full-service portrait photography business based here in Longmont
 .</p><p>Follow her on social media at @AmberCantornaWylde and learn more ab
 out her advocacy work at AmberCantornaWylde.com and her photography busines
 s at WyldeandFreePhotography.com.</p><p><br></p><p>Saturday- May 16- Bring
 your homies and make some gnomies...In this beginner clay class\, you'll le
 arn the basics of clay hand building\, then we will build a gnome and if th
 ere is time\, a mushroom house! We'll talk about fantastical worlds and bui
 lding spaces where everyone can feel safe. You will come back to glaze afte
 r we bisque fire it in 1 week. </p><p><br></p><p>Saturday- May 23- Mandala
 Painting- Tap into your creativity during this meditative painting class us
 ing acrylics. The word ‘mandala’ is a Sanskrit word meaning “circle” or “ce
 nter”. Many different cultures around the world use mandalas in their spiri
 tual practice. We'll sketch our mandala and then paint with acrylics using
 a dotting method. Manifest your state of mind through shapes\, colors and p
 atterns and center yourself in the process.</p><p><br></p><p>Saturday- May
 30- Glaze your gnomies- this is a low key class where gnomes and mushroom h
 ouses can be glazed.<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260206T232633Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pride Arts Sampler
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
