BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20251023T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20251023T210000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;COUNT=7;BYDAY=TH
EXDATE;TZID=America/Denver:20251127T180000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:4ptht3qku9qhb9ansb8p6m330s@google.com
CREATED:20250825T145641Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><h1><b>Sign up- </b><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=h
 ttps://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/16033
 23&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1756565782972277&amp\;usg=AOvVaw
 1ldSolYH2YxiEMgVwqIt1z" target="_blank">Firehouse Art Center - Continuing W
 heel Throwing (6 week session)</a></h1><br><br><h4>Thu\, Oct 23\, 2025 - De
 c 4\, 2025<br></h4><br><br><br><br><br><br>6:00pm - 9:00pm MDT<br><br><br><
 br><br>Instructor- Valerie L.<br><br><br><br><br>Meet your instructor- Vale
 rie Langlois<br><p>My name is Val\, and I’m a small batch\, ceramic artist
 based in Longmont. Though I work full-time as a data scientist\, I explore
 throwing different forms on the wheel\, new surface decoration techniques\,
  and glaze chemistry in my free time.</p><p><br></p><p>This course is desig
 ned for students who have taken a prior beginner or intermediate wheel-thro
 wing class\, and want to strengthen and improve their skills. Prior wheel-t
 hrowing experience is required. We will start the session identifying skill
 s that each student wants to improve on (e.g.\, pulling walls\, creating sp
 ecific forms\, exploring surface decoration techniques\, handles\, etc.) or
  a specific project (e.g.\, teapot\, plate\, butter crock). The rest of the
  session will be used to work on these skills and/or projects.</p><p><br></
 p><p>3 hours\, 1 day a week\, for 6 weeks\, in a group of up to 5. $280\, A
 ge 18+</p><p>No classes on Thanksgiving and we will return for the last wee
 k on December 4th</p><p><br></p><p>Classes meet once a week for 3 hours in
 the FAC Ceramics Studio for six weeks (18 hours of total instruction)\, and
  are limited in size to 5 students. Access to open studio hours is included
  for the duration of the class and two week following. While communal tools
  are available\, a basic tool kit will also need to be purchased at the sta
 rt of the session. You can purchase here-<a href="https://www.google.com/ur
 l?q=https://firehouseart.org/product/tool-kit/.&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calen
 dar&amp\;ust=1756565782972277&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2B8n2NbP45h_U3eRKcBw23" target
 ="_blank">https://firehouseart.org/product/tool-kit/.</a></p><p><br></p><p>
 A 20 lb bag of clay is provided to each student\, along with a half-shelf a
 nd cubby. Additional clay is available for purchase.</p><p><br></p><p>Studi
 o classes are for adults ages 18 and over (students 16+ may attend classes
 when accompanied by a paying adult).</p><p><br></p><p>Refunds are not allow
 ed after the course begins. Refunds requested during the week prior to the
 start of the class will be honored at 50%. If you would like to request a r
 efund\, email <a href="mailto:education@firehouseart.org" target="_blank">e
 ducation@firehouseart.org</a>.<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250825T145651Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Continuing Wheel Throwing (6 week session)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
