BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20251102T200000Z
DTEND:20251102T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:2cpcq4bl564iibv7e1pkqatisq@google.com
CREATED:20250926T204125Z
DESCRIPTION:<h1><strong>COMMUNITY STORY SHARE</strong></h1><h1><span>Novemb
 er 2\, 1pm-3pm</span></h1><h1>Stories that spark connection\, traditions th
 at teach future generation and memories that make us who we are.</h1><h1>Su
 bmit your interest to present here- <a href="https://forms.gle/B2ZHxkdxZSxD
 ezXf8" target="_blank">https://forms.gle/B2ZHxkdxZSxDezXf8</a></h1><p>Join
 us this Day of the Dead season to remember our loved ones. In the tradition
  of communing with those whose spirits are with us\, we invite you to share
  your stories of them in community. Speakers will have 7 minutes to share\,
  and may include up to 20 slides or mementos with their stories.</p><p><str
 ong>Open Call for stories\, anecdotes\, memories\, traditions\, etc.</stron
 g></p><p>We are seeking out people who have a story to share about their an
 cestors. Mixing short commentary\, images\, food (if applicable) and presen
 tation slides\, the speaker gets to talk about things they love in a short\
 , visual and creative format.</p><p>Community Story Share is similar to the
  Pecha Kucha event we used to host but the focus is on family traditions an
 d memories for October.</p><p>The Day of the Dead\, or Día de los Muertos\,
  is a vibrant celebration that transcends mere remembrance\, weaving a rich
  tapestry of cultural significance and familial bonds. This Mexican traditi
 on invites families to honor their deceased loved ones through colorful alt
 ars\, heartfelt offerings\, and joyous gatherings. At the heart of this cel
 ebration lies the profound importance of family stories\, which serve as a
 vital link between generations\, imbuing the festivities with personal mean
 ing and emotional resonance.</p><p>As families come together to share tales
  of those who have passed\, they participate in a timeless ritual that not
 only preserves memories but also fosters a sense of belonging and continuit
 y. These oral traditions are instrumental in shaping identities\, allowing
 younger generations to connect with their heritage while providing a source
  of comfort and healing. In this exploration\, we delve into the multifacet
 ed role that family stories play in the Day of the Dead\, highlighting thei
 r significance in both cultural preservation and personal connection.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251029T204851Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Community Story Share
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
