DESCRIPTION:<br><br><br><br><h1><b>Mixed Media Workshop- Exploring Abstract
 ion Through Collage</b></h1><br><b>Sign up here- </b><a href="https://www.h
 isawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1951799?source=al
 l-activities">Firehouse Art Center - Mixed Media Workshop- Exploring Abstra
 ction Through Collage</a><br><br><h4>16 – 18+ yrs<br>Sat\, Jul 18\, 2026<br
 >9:00am - 12:00pm MDT</h4><br><br><br><br><br><br>Create an intuitive abstr
 act collage on a gallery-wrapped canvas using acrylic paint\, archival pape
 rs\, matte medium\, and mark-making techniques. Through guided exercises\,
 demonstrations\, and experimentation\, students will explore layering\, com
 position\, color\, texture\, and visual movement while developing confidenc
 e in an intuitive creative process. No prior experience is required.<br><p>
 <br></p><p>Class + Materials Fee: $20 (includes gallery-wrapped canvas\, pa
 ints\, papers\, matte medium\, and shared tools)</p><p>Meet your instructor
 :</p><p>Mollie Jackson (she/her) is a Longmont-based artist whose large-sca
 le abstract paintings pulse with energy. Working intuitively\, she builds l
 ayered surfaces through paint\, expressive mark-making\, and collage\, tran
 slating raw emotion into visual form.</p><p>She earned her BFA from the Uni
 versity of Iowa and apprenticed with the Chair of Sculpture at the Art Inst
 itute of Chicago\, refining her understanding of form and process. Raised i
 n a home shaped by her mother’s abstract painting practice\, she developed
 an early and lasting connection to the studio.</p><p>Jackson has presented
 solo exhibitions across Colorado and is the summer artist in residence at t
 he Firehouse Art Center in summer 2026.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260713T152702Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mixed Media Workshop- Exploring Abstraction Through Collage
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
