DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- <a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-c
 enter-1/schedules/activity-set/1794863?source=all-activities">Firehouse Art
  Center - Wood Workers Camp</a><br>Ages 6-12<br><p><strong><b>Instructor:</
 b></strong> Amy Lummus<br></p><p>Wood Workers Camp is an immersive\, hands-
 on making experience designed for curious\, capable kids who love to build\
 , tinker\, and create with intention. Campers work with a wide range of rea
 l materials and tools — including wood\, fasteners\, sandpaper\, hand saws\
 , screwdrivers\, measuring tools\, and paint — learning how to plan\, const
 ruct\, revise\, and finish their own original projects.</p><p>As campers de
 monstrate readiness\, they are introduced to hand tools and basic construct
 ion techniques\, with a strong emphasis on responsibility\, care\, and resp
 ect for tools and shared space.</p><p><br></p><p>Throughout the week we lis
 ten to music\, get messy\, and fully engage in the tactile joy of making. P
 rojects may include sculptural builds\, functional objects\, signs\, and im
 aginative constructions driven by each child’s interests. The camp conclude
 s with a small “art show\,” where campers proudly present their finished wo
 rk to peers and families\, celebrating both process and creativity.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260207T000514Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Wood Workers Camp
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
