UID:2tvalr9m2a7cmo4in5ll2fmfpr@google.com
CREATED:20260123T234941Z
DESCRIPTION:Sign up here- <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www
 .hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1784936&amp\;sa
 =D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1769644161380740&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1zFLYjPucW
 4cgPCLDeZ_Oq" target="_blank">Firehouse Art Center - Intermediate Crochet-
 2nd Sundays</a><br><br><br><br><p>Crochet in the Round - take your beginner
  crochet skills to the next level by learning how to crochet in the round.
 This unlocks all sorts of projects including flat round shapes like coaster
 s and scrubbies\, to 3D shapes like amigurumi and plushies. Participants sh
 ould have beginner knowledge on how to crochet in a row. Target skills for
 this class include: magic ring\, increases\, invisible decreases\, invisibl
 e join. You are welcome to bring your own materials if you have them (hook\
 , yarn\, stitch markers\, scissors\, tapestry/darning needle). Hooks\, yarn
 \, and stitch markers will be available for purchase in class ($5 materials
  fee to be collected at the beginning of class- cash or check).<br><br>Meet
  our instructor:<br>Kathleen is a hospice music therapist who loves to croc
 het. She learned how to crochet during the pandemic to help develop healthy
  coping skills and a new hobby. Kathleen enjoys creating meaningful crochet
  pieces including custom dog and cat ornaments and plushies. Kathleen has e
 xperience teaching music to all ages (K-12\, college level\, and an 84 year
  old who wanted to learn bassoon)\, and is branching out now to teaching cr
 ochet in her local community. When she’s not crocheting\, she enjoys spendi
 ng time with her husband and three greyhounds\, traveling\, gardening\, and
  listening to music.<br><br>Class Fee: $25<br>Minimum 1\, Maximum 4<br><br>
 These sessions are open and working on skills that build upon the beginners
  class that Amber Ivey teaches.<br><br>Skill level: adventurous beginner<br
 ><br>Age Range: HS and older. HS students require parent to be in attendanc
 e</p><p></p><br><br><h3>Class Requirements</h3><br><ul><li>Participants und
 er 15yrs of age must be accompanied by a paid and participating adult.</li>
 </ul><br><br><h3>Other Things To Know</h3><br><br><u></u><br><br>Adult Part
 icipation<br><br>Required.<br><p>Paid and participating adult required for
 children Under 16</p><br><br><u></u><br><br>Cancellation Policy<br><br><p>R
 efund policy: Fees can be refunded with a 48 hour notification before the s
 tart of the first class in a session or 48 hours before the class.</p><hr><
 br><br><h2>What To Bring</h2><br><ul><li>You are welcome to bring your own
 materials if you have them (hook\, yarn\, stitch markers\, scissors\, tapes
 try/darning needle).</li><li>Hooks\, yarn\, and stitch markers will be avai
 lable for purchase in class ($5 materials fee to be collected at the beginn
 ing of class- cash or check).</li></ul>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260608T222946Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intermediate Crochet
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
