BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260509T190000Z
DTEND:20260509T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:1rv0mlrn5toentsj30a797qb4t@google.com
CREATED:20260206T233016Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Sign up for the whole session here- <a href="https://www.his
 awyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1802421"><u>Firehou
 se Art Center - Pride Month Art Sampler</u></a></p><p>We are partnering wit
 h the Longmont Library and Butterscotch Studios to present an art exhibit f
 or Pride to show at the library on June 7th.  The pieces in the show will b
 e created over a series of 5 art classes at the Firehouse.  The whole progr
 am only costs $100! You will have a chance to experience different mediums
 from acrylic\, to clay\, to fabric! All abilities welcome- no artistic expe
 rience necessary! (Age 14+) </p><p>May 3 (FIRST CLASS IS ON SUNDAY)- Let yo
 ur freak flag fly- Create your own flag or banner that represents you! You'
 ll learn what makes a "good" flag (keep it simple silly!) and create one th
 at is all about you.  You'll get to take that flag home to fly proudly.</p>
 <p>Saturday- May 9- 1:30- 3:30- The Art of Healing: A guided Artistic Exper
 ience</p><p>Experience the power of art to unlock healing and transformatio
 n.  This introspective artistic activity will incorporate meditative practi
 ces and personal introspection with ceramic painting\, inviting you to fost
 er connection within yourself and with those around you to create something
  beautiful.  </p><p>Meet your instructor- Amber Cantorna-Wylde (she/her) is
  a national speaker\, consultant\, and community healer passionate about fo
 stering a world of acceptance and belonging. She’s the author of three book
 s\, the founder the Unashamed Love Collective which ran for 10 seasons\, an
 d she now owns a full-service portrait photography business based here in L
 ongmont.</p><p>Follow her on social media at @AmberCantornaWylde and learn
 more about her advocacy work at AmberCantornaWylde.com and her photography
 business at WyldeandFreePhotography.com.</p><p>Saturday- May 16- Bring your
  homies and make some gnomies...In this beginner clay class\, you'll learn
 the basics of clay hand building\, then we will build a gnome and if there
 is time\, a mushroom house! We'll talk about fantastical worlds and buildin
 g spaces where everyone can feel safe. You will come back to glaze after we
  bisque fire it in 1 week. </p><p>Saturday- May 23- Mandala Painting- Tap i
 nto your creativity during this meditative painting class using acrylics. T
 he word ‘mandala’ is a Sanskrit word meaning “circle” or “center”. Many dif
 ferent cultures around the world use mandalas in their spiritual practice.
 We'll sketch our mandala and then paint with acrylics using a dotting metho
 d. Manifest your state of mind through shapes\, colors and patterns and cen
 ter yourself in the process.</p><p>Saturday- May 30- Glaze your gnomies- th
 is is a low key class where gnomes and mushroom houses can be glazed.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260206T233016Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pride Arts Sampler
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
