DESCRIPTION:Sign up here: <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www
 .hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1993334&amp\;sa
 =D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1787357189427716&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3afSm2JP_g
 sa3WrOxgrGdr" target="_blank">Firehouse Art Center - Viva la Vulva</a><br><
 br><p>You’re invited to embrace body positivity through clay\, crafting you
 r own vulva-shaped tissue box as a bold\, functional art piece that you can
  take home after it is fired. This empowering experience celebrates our ana
 tomy in a safe\, supportive\, inclusive setting where creativity and self-a
 cceptance take center stage. This workshop is for female-identifying people
 .  <br><br>$70 </p><p>Age Range: Adults 18+<br></p><p>2 classes</p><p>1st c
 lass- 2 hours</p><p>2nd class- 1 hour</p><p>Location- Upstairs classroom</p
 ><p><br></p><p>Karrie Steely is an artist\, instructor\, and arts community
  builder. She is passionate about sharing the gifts of a lifelong commitmen
 t to creativity and curiosity. Collaborators\, cohorts and students alike a
 re inspired by her joy and enthusiasm.</p><p> </p><p>Karrie’s award-winning
  artwork has been exhibited in Colorado\, Nebraska and Kansas. So far\, 202
 6 projects have included an artist residency at the Robert Henri Museum and
  Gallery where she taught workshops\, leading community murals in Nebraska\
 , and judging at the Nebraska State Fair. She was a 2023-2025 Rural Regener
 ator Fellow with Springboard for the Arts. She recently moved back to her n
 ative Colorado\, where she continues to lead workshops and paint murals.</p
 >
LAST-MODIFIED:20260817T175817Z
