RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;UNTIL=20260820T055959Z;BYDAY=3TH
EXDATE;TZID=America/Denver:20260219T183000
EXDATE;TZID=America/Denver:20260618T183000
EXDATE;TZID=America/Denver:20260716T183000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:5ntjsjjpn2ddlh85q1ravvksg9@google.com
CREATED:20250904T205029Z
DESCRIPTION:Sign Up- <a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-art-center
 -1/schedules/activity-set/1603368?source=all-activities">Firehouse Art Cent
 er - "How to Play in the Dark with Art"</a><br><br><h2><b>Class Experience<
 /b></h2><br><p></p><p>"How to Play in the Dark with Art" Come explore the p
 ower of art making to move through the challenges\, blocks\, and wounds tha
 t we can't really run away from (even if we try to). When we have the tools
  to move through our struggles\, it opens you up to a whole new path forwar
 d.  You will be invited into a therapeutic art experience utilizing presenc
 e\, curiosity\, compassion\, play\, imagination\, and creative expression.
  Come on\, you know you are curious…I love to say that art is an experiment
  and you never know what you will learn along the way. Maybe you will disco
 ver something about yourself that you have been looking for. And creating i
 n community makes it even more powerful and rich. If your inner-critic is h
 olding you back\, know that NO ART EXPERIENCE IS NEEDED!!! AND ALL ART MATE
 RIALS ARE PROVIDED!!! Just bring your curious mind and playful spirit. Resi
 stance and fear is also welcome.</p><p>________________________<br>About th
 e Facilitator:<br>Danielle Rifkin\, LPC\, ATR is the owner of How To Play I
 n The Dark. She is a Somatic\, Art &amp\; Play Therapist\, and Grief Ritual
 ist. She has been running grief circles\, art groups\, and other experienti
 al offerings for over a decade. She got her Master's degree from Naropa Uni
 versity in Transpersonal Psychology and has worked in a variety of therapeu
 tic settings in her career. She has facilitated hundreds of groups where sh
 e emphasizes creating spaces that allow for authenticity and feeling safe e
 nough to show all parts of themselves.<br><br><br>Cost- $40 (Sliding scale
 is available by reaching out to <a href="mailto:daniellerifkin@riseuprooted
 .org" target="_blank">daniellerifkin@riseuprooted.org</a>)</p><p>Materials
 provided<br>Age: 18+<br>Minimum: 3 students Maximum: 12 students<br>No expe
 rience needed</p><p>Refunds if cancellations are made 48+ hours in advance<
 /p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260816T160544Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:How to Play in the Dark with Art
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
