DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20260213T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20260213T200000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:ceabkp142b3h0cr9v82gvvugq2@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Denver:20260206T180000
CREATED:20250430T000231Z
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy live music and refreshments available for donation. All r
 eceptions are free and open to the public.<br><br>"SECONDS”<br>DOUG FELKLEY
  ARTIST IN RESIDENCY CULMINATION EXHIBIT<br>FEBRUARY 13- MARCH 8\, 2026<br>
 ARTIST TALK: FEB 22: 3PM- 5PM<br>Reception Details<br>5pm-6pm- Masks requir
 ed in Main and South Gallery<br>6pm-8pm- Masks required in South Gallery<br
 >(Gallery will have masks available)<br>The Firehouse Art Center invites yo
 u to Doug Felkley’s<br>culminating exhibition. Felkley was selected as the
 2025/6<br>Winter Artist in Residence for the Firehouse Artist Occupied<br>S
 eries. This program invites emerging and established artists<br>working in
 all media to explore their practice while engaging<br>with the community. T
 he artist utilizes the Firehouse South<br>Gallery as a working studio for t
 hree months before a<br>culminating solo exhibition in the Main Gallery.<br
 >The title of this exhibit\, “Seconds\,” is a reference to many things. Sec
 ond careers\, second chances for found objects\,<br>second opportunities to
  teach\, as well as the passage of time — second by second.<br>Using bent w
 ood lamination techniques\, Felkley creates sculptures using multiple layer
 s of thin material glued<br>together. These layers are bent into the desire
 d shape. Felkley then uses pressure\, created by vacuum or through<br>tape
 binding\, to finish the shape. The more layers in each lamination\, the str
 onger the piece will be.<br>Doug Felkley is a teacher\, a sculptor\, and a
 sometimes reluctant furniture maker. After retiring from a decades long car
 eer as a gymnastics coach\, Felkley felt it was time to explore an entirely
  new second career. This desire for something new led Felkley to study fine
  furniture making and design at Red Rocks Community College. Upon completio
 n of the program he began taking commissions for custom furniture pieces\,
 something that he found extremely stressful. Looking for a new creative out
 let\, Felkley began experimenting with wood focused sculpture and<br>found
 expression for his creative ideas. Although he felt deeply connected to his
  new creative path\, Felkley missed working with students\, and out of nowh
 ere an opportunity to be a middle school woodworking teacher showed up!<br>
 Now\, teaching woodworking as an art form gives Felkley an outlet for both
 of his passions\, teaching and art.<br>Seconds II- South Gallery<br>Works b
 y Jean Hultkrans and kelly j drumright<br>Curated by Doug Felkley<br>“Secon
 ds II”\, curated by Winter Artist in Residence\, Doug Felkley is an exhibit
  that explores transformation. Rather than separating practices by medium o
 r theme\, the gallery is arranged to allow kelly drumright's sculptural ass
 emblages and Jean Hultkrans’ collages and ikebana to face and echo one anot
 her across the room.<br>The installation emphasizes cycles—of use and reuse
 \, of knowing and not knowing\, of injury and repair—creating visual and em
 otional connections between two distinct practices. By placing altered medi
 cal materials beside layered images and organic forms\, the gallery becomes
  a space where vulnerability\, resilience\, and renewal coexist. This share
 d environment invites viewers to move slowly\, notice connections\, and exp
 erience the quiet power of second chances and second readings.<br>Music pro
 vided by Finn O'Sullivan <br><a href="https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=https%
 3A%2F%2Ffirehouseart.org%2Fexhibitions%2Fupcoming-exhibitions%3Ffbclid%3DIw
 AR1qt0c0IeNEIdUEt_NjtX6yxR2D5UW_DQOj3_Ncjkq4-_zj7ZYAoctJEoY&h=AT1-4Gtoz_ADK
 2jyEjNWQyNigk7CX2-IwOrR7-PiAfYHWJBGp847P5nxMSA6807kC-YSdVPz5JGr1mog8DezVyPg
 _jB00UNcQkgNUKach4bzy4q9AdIncd0HXxj2GOBw5Q&__tn__=q&c[0]=AT2U2D0xK8jj1MHxGc
 KXc8n3lzN0A4NyHMyMbRte1PxzAxkzZnGg8x03JXp5H_FCNK50-omllz-yBM4CuoPtMP27dNRxc
 WH6HDMQoKVOGcE09-AJ6F2V31cCqzdXGdqbQJCuxIGbDxZsZmy5ioMhbXgs3xj1rdO9nRkU3C2L
 duM1bL_Z" target="_blank">https://firehouseart.org/exhibitions/upcoming-exh
 ibitions</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260504T213517Z
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:2nd Friday Exhibit Opening-
