BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20251206T170000Z
DTEND:20251206T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:6v0p3odmfdmpkv6j3j777vtpom@google.com
CREATED:20251117T154426Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>"Bending Wood"   </p><p><br>2 day workshop- you must attend
 Dec 6 and 7th workshops</p><p><a href="https://www.hisawyer.com/firehouse-a
 rt-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1695415" target="_blank">https://www.his
 awyer.com/firehouse-art-center-1/schedules/activity-set/1695415</a></p><p>T
 his two day adult workshop will explore the art of bending wood using the f
 ree-form bent lamination technique.  Participants will create unique shapes
  that will be included in a community art piece exhibited at the Firehouse
 during the Winter Residency culminating exhibit.  Following the exhibit\, p
 articipants will be able to take their creations home.  </p><p><br></p><p>$
 50/person includes all materials and supplies\,  5-10 participants\, no pri
 or woodworking experience needed</p><p><br></p><p>Meet your instructor</p><
 p>Doug Felkley:</p><p>I am a teacher\, a sculptor\, and a sometimes relucta
 nt furniture maker.  After retiring from a decades long career as a gymnast
 ics coach\, I felt it was time to explore an entirely new second career.  T
 his desire for something new led me to study fine furniture making and desi
 gn at Red Rocks Community College.  Upon completion of the program I began
 taking commissions for custom furniture pieces\, something that I found ext
 remely stressful.  Looking for a new creative outlet\, I began experimentin
 g with wood focused sculpture and found expression for my creative ideas.  
 Although I felt deeply connected to this creative path\, I missed working w
 ith kids\, and out of nowhere an opportunity to be a middle school woodwork
 ing teacher showed up!  Now\, teaching woodworking as an art form gives me
 an outlet for both of my passions\, teaching and art.  </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251117T154506Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bending Wood Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20250509T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20250509T200000
DTSTAMP:20261030T045920Z
UID:2p67acr2vmpda72bc570vl02ek@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Denver:20250509T173000
CREATED:20250430T000231Z
DESCRIPTION:MYTH AND MEMORY: LYNDEN CLINE AND JEFF LEAKE\nMAY 2\, 2025- JUN
 E 15\, 2025\nEXHIBIT RECEPTION- MAY 9\, 6PM-8PM\n$5 suggested donation\nMyt
 h and Memory brings together Lynden Cline and Jeff Leake\, two artists who
 navigate the spaces between personal history and cultural myth\, between ob
 served reality and imagined landscapes. Through painting\, sculpture\, and
 visual storyteling\, these works reflect on how history—both colective and
 deeply personal—shapes our present. Together\, these artists invite us into
  a world where myth and memory blur\, where storyteling is both a personal
 act of reflection and a cultural force shaping our understanding of the pas
 t and present.\n\nSOUTH GALLERY\nVONALDA UTTERBACK\, PATTY FABIAN- MAY 9\n\
 nVonalda Utterback is a Longmont-based mixed media artist and texture queen
  who enjoys learning new techniques and approaches while searching out inte
 resting materials and\ndiscovering new textures to incorporate into her wor
 k. Her approach is grounded in abstract realism\, offering a visual languag
 e that speaks to the heart as well as the mind.\n\nPatricia Fabian was born
  in Chicago\, Illinois in 1957. She received a BFA in Graphic Design from t
 he University of Illinois in 1981. Her 45 year career in design greatly enh
 anced her understanding of color theory\, hierarchy\, and composition. Thes
 e concepts greatly influence her artwork today as well as the precision and
  accuracy required of her early medical art education.\n\nMusic Provided by
  Meryk Sackrison
LAST-MODIFIED:20260504T213517Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:2nd Friday Exhibit Opening- Myth and Memory: Lynden Cline and Jeff
 Leake
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
